        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #1',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"The Black Cat"</p><p>There is this black cat that always stumble at the front door of Tatay\'s house. Sometimes, it just wanders around the parking space. It\'s always looking for food because it\'s hungry. I used to think this black cat is rude just like the gray cat that always sneaks from the open hole by our roof to enter the house and make messes in our kitchen. But no, this one is very kind. So I grew my likeness for this cat because it\'s quiet and doesn\'t get scared easily (compared to other cats who runs away even if you\'re not that close to it). I approach the cat with no harm intentions. It won\'t run away as long as I walk up to it.</p><p>I hear the cat out the front door saying "meow" usually at lunchtime. I always give it something to eat, especially if I\'m the last person still eating my meal. When no one is looking, I share a piece of my meal to the cat. The cat would exclaim "meow" and start to eat the food. I kept on doing this as long as no one will see me and until I get tired of it. I pity the cat and because I know it is a kind cat, I have respect for the cat. It feels good when we make something happy. Not only were we are able to give them happiness, the happiness goes back to us.</p><p>There were 2 instances the black cat went to the house. One instance was that she puked/<span style="text-decoration:underline;">lose her lunch</span> in our kitchen. I got mad for that. The second instance was that I accidentally left our gate opened, the cat went inside the house. I went down to turn on the switch for our water tank so that I can reserve water for the next day. When I was walking back to our stairway, the black cat stumbled on our gate sitting and giving me a cold stare. I was surprised because I had no idea how it got there only to realize it went inside the house by sneaking silently. Ninja moves!</p><p>Noel told me that Megan\'s friend owns the cat. I wonder why it always goes to our place other than the fact that it\'s hungry. It should stay home and be taken care of. The cat seems astray as if she has no place to stay. The owner should look after it and avoid that from being a stray cat who frequently wanders around looking for food or just staying under the vehicles.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 2, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-10-02',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #2',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"A Rare Opportunity"</p><p>Being a fan (a follower, not the object) of a known personality is fun. If you are this famous person, having fans can make you popular because they admire you and looks up to you as a person not common to other people. But how about meeting them personally and having a chance to take a picture with them? The feeling is amazing! This is exactly what happened to me. Being a gaming aficionado, I was able to meet a then-GM of Mercenaries Online PH when they held a LAN tournament at Baguio. She was GM Rhaine, a former GM of Crossfire PH, a rival online game of where she is working then.</p><p>The tournament was at Chips Internet Cafe on Lower Session Road (beside 7-11 and CID) on February 16, 2013. They had a freeplay the day before the tournament was held, where I played their game for 1 hour to try it out. I also played just to see GM Rhaine personally because I really wanted to see her and nothing else. In tournament day, I went to the shop early so I can see her again. Though I won\'t join the tournament because I don\'t play their game and because I just registered to try the game out, I spent my time simply spectating the teams that are playing. I looked like a fool just walking around and watching them because I\'m not leaving until I have a picture with her as a remembrance. GMs experienced brownout in the afternoon so I roamed around Lower Session and came back when the power returned. The tournament ended at around 6:30 PM and that\'s when me and GM Rhaine had a picture. I came home with a Mercenaries Online poster that even up to now, I still haven\'t unrolled it. That was one of the best days ever!</p><p>I liked her because she is sizzling hot. I have a crush on her. Her eyes are that of a cat and her smile kills me. Before we took a picture, she asked me if I was the one messaging her in FB. I said that it was me and she\'s glad that I came. When they left, I bid farewell and said that they should come again soon. She smiled. Then I came home happy for an opportunity like this is rare.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 2, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-10-06',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #3',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"The GameBoy Service"</p><p>Back in 2005, I had my first taste in doing business by lending my GameBoy Advance SP for a fee. I charge P1/min and time them so they know how much they\'ll pay. GameBoy Advance SP was a popular handheld console back then. It was me and my bestfriend Romeo who came up with this. He charges P2/min for his rental fee and he has more games than me. But because my rental fee is cheaper, our classmates would prefer me over Romeo haha! Even if he has GameBoy Color, I still beat him with my cheaper fee. My usual customers were Ivan, Sean, Paolo, Brian and Cristian whereas Ryzher (we weren\'t bestfriends yet) and Mark were Romeo\'s customers.</p><p>We did this for 1 week only, because I remember we were busy for the UN Day Celebration. There were no subjects, it was a week dedicated solely for UN Day practice. Sadly, it abruptly ended when Mama told me that the office got complaints of parents\' children having their money "wasted". At least it was good while it lasted. My earnings had a minimum of P100/day and I would always give it to Mama as my way of helping her. It was during this time that I learned how to be thrifty and to use money wisely.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 2, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-02-09',
        ]);

