        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Jogging, Exams, and Dates',
            'description' => '<p>A cold, rainy day surprises my Sunday morning. The planned jogging didn\'t push through. We were supposed to jog at 5:30 AM but we failed to wake up earlier. Me and Ate Kamille enjoyed the cold morning and decided to sleep more. I woke up at around 9 AM. Not the usual time I wake up. Haha!</p><p>This is my only day to review for Midterm exams starting tomorrow, Monday. Tomorrow\'s exam will be OOP 1 and Network Fundamentals. Laboratory and Lecture in one day. I fear my Network Fundamentals class. Questions will be arguably tougher than the Prelim exam. OOP 1\'s lecture is easy but the lab will be harder. Well, goodluck tomorrow then.</p><p>I texted Kaye and I said that we should have a date today. The plan is set in the afternoon. I wore my personally bought CM Punk\'s Best In The World (black) shirt, gray Tribal jeans bought by Daddy, a personally bought gray Vans sneakers and a pair of white Dickies socks. I went to Kaye\'s boarding house at Sandico St. (below Cathedral) only to find out she just woke up. I patiently waited for 30 minutes, just roaming around the parking area. Then I saw her coming out, she was sizzling hot! Happiness. Sadly, we fought at Vizco\'s (my first time to eat there) because I was laughing at her. It wasn\'t a negative joke but she deemed it negative. I won\'t say something that would hurt her. I just didn\'t realize she would take it seriously. She made me cry because she wouldn\'t hear my side, that she always must be right and I couldn\'t justify my own actions. By her request, she wants to be alone and I need to leave. When I got home, I cried really hard. Then I took a nap silently.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 12, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-08-03',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'The Breakdown',
            'description' => '<p>Today is Monday and marks the 10th week of the current trimester. Finally, we started our Finals lecture on OOP 1. A delayed meeting is precious enough to catch up with discussions since there\'s less than a month left and its the Final exams already. It\'s too fast!</p><p>I was supposed to see Kaye today but she didn\'t allow me since her "roommate" is there. I respect her privacy but I felt like she just doesn\'t want to see me today. Quite sad to know that I can\'t go to the boarding house. Then she asked me (via text) if I\'m having a hard time with her, how my efforts go in vain and she doesn\'t reciprocate it, how the relationship affects my studies, how unfair that she doesn\'t give an attention to me, that she couldn\'t reply back to me and if I am already "tired". I asked her if she still loves me and she said "Kaw ba?". She didn\'t really answer it. When I said "Love you baby.", she replied "Ok.. sige kain ka na. Ingat.". I still have to ask about it so she would say she loves me too. From this point, I felt sad. Moreover, when I made it to Loakan terminal, I called her and she said they\'re in a taxi going to Loakan already. I told her to text me before she leaves. She probably just didn\'t care how I persevered waiting for her.</p><p>I decided to print 8 photos of me and Kaye. While I was waiting, tears ran down my face. I went home and immediately sat on the couch. Never before had I cried that emotionally when she can\'t say she loves me. I had to ask her before she can say it without being told to. One day, she would realize that even in my busy classes, I care, I pity and I love her no matter what happens. It truly pains me that she wouldn\'t talk to me the way she used to do before.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 12, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-08-11',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Early Bird Catches the Worm',
            'description' => '<p>Woke up at around 4:12 AM. Had around a 6-hr sleep. I scheduled this day for my jogging since I need to be innovative and creative during my 3 weeks of semestral break. Heated my water, took a bath, dressed up, had wax, prepared the items to bring (wallet, face towel, cellphone, perfume, water) and placed them in a Reebok bag that Ate Kamille lent me temporarily.</p><p>Time check at 5:26 AM. Got the house keys and carried my bag. Ooohh, it\'s not a cold morning (when it\'s supposed to be). I hardly feel anything on my Kevin Garnett Adidas shoes. Anyway, I made it to Burnham and had a warm-up by the Children\'s Park going to the Biking Area and to the Lake, at last. I was there just in time for 6 AM (the bell from City Hall rang) and jogged around the Lake for 9 laps. That beats my July 29 record with only 8 1/2 laps. Black shoes are better than white ones haha.</p><p>After jogging, I went to TNC only to find out it was closed. Well, I can\'t play today haha. Despite that, I enjoyed so much.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 12, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-09-07',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Good Food, Bad Brother',
            'description' => '<p>A cold breeze greets my Thursday morning. I was able to prepare and eat breakfast in less than an hour since I\'m rushing to my 7:30 class (Applied Data Structures). The jeep filled up so fast, expecting to arrive in UC in time. I realized I was too early because Ma\'am Cruz isn\'t around yet. As expected, Ricky, Kendrick and Jhon didn\'t attend class again. Paul came around 8:30 AM, 25 minutes before the time. At least he still bothered to enter class. But it was vice-versa for Communication in the Workplace: Paul was absent and the 3 friends were present. So ironic.</p><p>After my Communication in the Workplace class, I waited for Ate Kamille and Ate Collen at 4:30 PM. We took a jeepney ride going to SLU (Ate Kamille and Ate Collen reminisces their tenure in SLU) and ate at Macsbox. I tried the Porky Pick rice and went for another round this time, ordered Crab Sticks rice. Delicious!</p><p>We went home then I ate Sopas, to make it up to Tita Vina who was expecting me since 4 PM (I wasn\'t able to text her). Again, I exclaimed inside my head "Delicious!". It is worth eating for. Mama called to ask how everything is going on the house. I said our woes with Patrick such as disrespecting our relatives, not eating meals on time, hard to call and the worst of them all, not attending classes. Oh for Pete\'s sake, Daddy should fund his schooling (personal needs too) when Patrick studies in Manila. He\'s a pain in the ass! I always get concerns from Tatay and Tita Vina about his laziness. I\'m already ashamed of answering their questions everytime they open it. Damn, my life is full of lies and problems!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 18, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-11-13',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'A Night to Remember',
            'description' => '<p>Kamile invited me to go out for a party at Spade Superclub a couple of days ago. I wore a plain black V-neck shirt, a Wall Street brown windbreaker, a Cotton Crews brown pants and the Converse sneakers. Also included is an undercut hairstyle, waxed by Bench. This is going to be a cold, cold night!</p><p>I arrived at Spade before 10 PM. I thought I was late since the agreement was 9:30 PM but it was exactly the opposite - I was early! I waited for around 40 minutes and they finally arrived. This is the 3rd time I\'ve been to Spade with her. March 29 was the first one, which was a CEA Night. August 20 was the second one, which was her 20th birthday and VIP inclusion.</p><p>Once inside, we ordered the first 2 buckets of San Mig Light worth P119 each - my treat but I assure them they\'ll pay the succeeding buckets because they didn\'t bother sharing their payment. Why go to a bar if you can\'t have your share for the beers?</p><p>Ange volunteered to pay for the 3rd bucket and asked me to bring it to our tables. I had to traverse the crowded space with ease since I was holding the bucket. Then some of Kamile\'s friends asked her if I\'m her boyfriend (how I\'d wish!). I said no since I heard them. This is one of the best moments of my night.</p><p>Two more of her friends came in. They\'re sisters! I socialized with one of them. Her name is Daphne. She wore a red cocktail dress, has semi-long hair and brought with her a small purse. At first, I thought she\'s sexy but as I gradually remember her face, she\'s not that sexy. Two foreigners came to our table. One of them is dancing with her. Then Daphne approached me and said she doesn\'t like it. So she talked to that foreigner and told him I\'m her boyfriend before telling it to me. It was her way to stop that guy from dancing with her. I just reluctantly agreed so I deemed her my "girlfriend of the night". It was just temporary! Haha. Another best moment of the night.</p><p>Ange then talked to me and asked if we would order a vodka (because the others aren\'t giving their share) or order another bucket instead. We went for Jose Cuervo (it was the cheapest one in the menu) and finally, the others gave their share. Kamile and Dave left during this time. Two of their friends left shortly afterwards. By this time, I socialized with one of the girls that was left behind.</p><p>Her name is Krizia. She used to be Kamile\'s classmate but transferred to UB taking up HRM. She asked me to keep the guy behind her at bay because she doesn\'t know him and he\'s not even part of our group. I convinced that person and he slowly went away. Good boy. We left Spade at around 4 AM. Daphne and her sister went home. This leaves 5 of us remaining. We walked going to the convenience store in Petron for relaxing since we got deaf due to the prolonged stay inside Spade. Ange was also drunk and was dancing dirty to me. It\'s a secret to not tell it to anyone we both know. I treated Krizia the Sola drink. We sat by the wooden bench and chatted until Ange, Mike (Ange\'s bestfriend) and one of Kamile\'s batchmate left. This leaves me and Krizia.</p><p>We didn\'t want to go home yet so we decided to chat in Rose Garden until sunlight. We got there by 5 AM. She has a crush on me! While chatting, I\'m so clingy and romantic to her (like holding her hands, wrapping my arms on her shoulder) as if she\'s my girlfriend. She\'s kind, funny and cute. At 6 AM, I hailed a cab for her and got her number (09174298800). Last best moment of the night. This is my best day for 2014!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-12-13',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Fresh Air and Fresh Starts: First Blog Post in 2015',
            'description' => '<p>We\'re 8 days removed from 2014. Everyone has had their ups and downs. I shared my own experience of the past year filled with lots of twists. A great year has passed.</p><p>Since December 29 last year (where me and Noel watched "The Amazing Praybeyt Benjamin" while Lola and Megan watched "Feng Shui" in SM), this is the 1st day of 2015 that I get to go outdoors. I\'ve been strained at home for over a week because I focused on cleaning the house (especially the windows).</p><p>At around 6:30 AM, I made it to Burnham Lake to jog for 8 laps. There were only a few joggers in the area, which made it easier for me to traverse around. After jogging, I bought 2 Powerade drinks at 7-11 to quench my thirst and sweat. It was fun. I rode a jeep going home afterwards. I played LOL until 2 PM where I will head to my next venture.</p><p>I wore my dark blue shorts for the first time (I bought it at the night market last year with Ate Kamille and Ate Collen) and my doll socks as well. Kamile is already in SM and I\'m still at the jeep. When I got there, she asked me where would she treat me for lunch. I gave her 5 choices: The Old Spaghetti House, Sizzling Plate, McDo, KFC and Pizza Hut. We agreed on KFC. Afterwards, I accompanied her in Watsons and in the foodcourt (she bought a new SUN sim). Then we went to Starbucks in Session Road and it\'s my turn to treat her. We both ordered the Christmas Cookie frappucinno, had a long convo and parted ways.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-01-08',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Enrollment in the Morning, Gaming Afterwards',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s a Monday morning today. The 1st day of enrollment for 3rd trimester SY 2014-2015 starts today. CAS, CCJE, CITCS and CCJE will start first. The schedule for CITCS is 3rd years (AM) and 2nd years (PM). Tomorrow are all 1st year students and on Wednesday, all year levels (plus transferees and shifters). Using the new plain black bag that Daddy bought, I set out to school. I grabbed my grades first and I was surprised. I passed Accounting Essentials! It was so unexpected! I\'m extremely happy but Jhon, Kendrick and Reyn failed. Jhon failed all his subjects except for OOP 2 and PE 3. Probably Kendrick failed his other subjects too and Reyn is taking up the 3rd trimester subjects tomorrow (she\'ll come back tomorrow). I\'m officially 2nd year and I think I won\'t be classmates with them for some time.</p><p>After enrolling, me and Kendrick had our haircuts. Then we went to Lemonet to play 2 games of LOL. We lost the 1st game but managed to win on the 2nd game.</p><p>I went home pretty late that they already ate for dinner. Then I realized that Daddy already left after 10 days of staying here. Another time.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-01-12',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'A Doorbell Facepalm Moment',
            'description' => '<p>Daddy arrived in the wee hours of Sunday, February 1st. I was still awake at 12 midnight yesterday but I wasn\'t able to witness his arrival. I knew it from Patrick since he was still awake that time (most of the time, he stays awake every midnight).</p><p>Today is the 3rd week of 3rd trimester SY 2014-2015. In Multimedia Systems lecture class, we\'re not even done with Chapter 1 yet. Exams will start in less than 3 weeks already haha! But were our discussions faster, we could have been in Chapter 2 by now. We are progressing in its lab class, finishing 3 activities (learning contract not included). In Systems Analysis and Design class, I hardly understand anything since we have to analyze a system, design it, maintain it for the company we selected (it\'s not fictitious, it\'s real!). Our Network Management is also fine. We\'re on our 2nd batch of lab activities, but on a turtle pace with the lectures.</p><p>I got home only to find out the screen door was locked. So I just texted my foreign friend about checking one of Tatay\'s vacant rooms. He came and said it was fine and he will inform me tomorrow about his decision. It\'s my 2nd time referring a possible transientee to Tatay. After eating, I finally got in! I asked Daddy why he locked the door and he said he was waiting for a doorbell. Damn, it was then that I realized that we have one! What a facepalm! Lesson learned? Utilize a doorbell to get in.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-02-02',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Andok\'s Talks With Classmates',
            'description' => '<p>A cold Thursday breeze greets me in the morning. Despite that, I wore my blue Cowboys polo and headed off to school at 9:18 AM. I went to the library and spent my time thinking and writing the idioms I\'m very familiar. I used my phone to connect to the school\'s Wi-Fi and managed to get in. Even if the webpage takes around 2 minutes to load, it was fine because I was able to get some idioms on the internet. At 10:20 AM, I left the library and headed off to my 1st class of the day: IT Presentation Skills.</p><p>We had a quiz on Technical Writing, including a spelling portion of 5 random words: insidious, magnanimous, quagmire, veracity, and wag. I got them all correct except for the last one, where I spelled it as "whag". I got a borderline score of 15/30 which was originally 14/30 due to a miscount. Luckily, I counted it off to double-check my score. I passed! After the class, me, Zel, Ric and Kevin decided to eat lunch together.</p><p>Ma\'am Kwo dismissed us immediately after the quiz since she has to attend a conference. We accompanied Zel on BPI first so she can withdraw money. Then we discussed on where we\'ll eat. We agreed on Andok\'s. From there, we all ordered the Porkcharap meal. Kevin treated the 1.5 L Coke, Zel treated the Mais Con Yelo and I treated the extra rice of 5. I spent P110 and it was worth it. We had a long, fun and exhilarating conversation together. The topics ranged from our past relationships, history of Facebook, UC\'s enrollment system and more.</p><p>I was so happy this day. How I\'d wish this happens again. A simple friends\' hangout can make an ordinary day so special! Hopefully, Zel will upload the selfies we took on Kevin\'s phone.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-02-05',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Missed Sales, Skipped Classes, and a KFC Bucket with Classmates',
            'description' => '<p>Yes, it\'s Saturday! Time is so fast! It doesn\'t feel like 2015 at all haha! Anyway, I stayed at the library to wait for my IT Presentation Skills class. For some reason, I couldn\'t think of what to write for over an hour of stay there. So I took a nap instead since I was still sleepy.</p><p>Prior going to school, I was at town by 7:39 AM to wait for the person who\'s going to buy my Tribal Camo shirt for P250. Although he never came, I was in at a surprise. The Session Road was closed due to CARAA, where schools from different places of CAR walk from Upper Session Road going to Baguio Athletic Bowl. I was at Porta Vaga and I just finished watching all the delegates before I went to UC. Despite not being able to sell my item, it was worth my time at Session Road.</p><p>At 10:20 AM, we waited for Ma\'am Kwo. When 15 minutes has passed, we already had an attendance paper to sign since she has not showed up for class. I still have another chance to do my assignment! So Zel and Ric wants to have lunch again so they told us about it and we agreed. This time, Kuya Wilson and Jules joined us.</p><p>We went to SM Baguio to stroll a bit and decided to eat at KFC. Zel and Ric ordered the Bucket Meal which has exactly 6 chickens for the 6 of us. Just like the Andok\'s 2 days ago, we took a lot of selfies (some were stolen shots) using Kevin\'s phone again. After eating, me, Kevin, Kuya Wilson and Jules went back to UC while Zel and Ric went home. Add this day to one of my happy days!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-02-07',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Chinese New Year 2015',
            'description' => '<p>Happy Chinese New Year! Thankfully, I have recovered from my colds (maybe because it\'s a holiday?). Which means there\'s also no classes today! Last night, I received an inquiry on my Ecko Ultd. polo at around 11 PM and he will buy it on Friday, which is tomorrow. Today, I received an inquiry each for my Mossimo shirt, Dolce &amp; Gabbana shirt and the Tender Juicy freebies. Now that\'s 3 customers (the 2 shirts were inquired by one person only). I\'m finally selling my clothes!</p><p>First up: the Mossimo and Dolce &amp; Gabbana shirts. We met up at our barangay\'s basketball court. He has a red, hatchback vehicle and I showed him my items. Then he asked me what else I\'m selling so I ran back home, took out the 2 shirts, got all the clothes and went back to his car. Inside, he scanned each clothes and eventually decided to buy the 2 shirts earlier because he didn\'t like the colors of my other clothes. So I ran back and got the 2 shirts. He bought it for a whopping P500! Sweet!</p><p>After the transaction, I went to town to sell my Tender Juicy freebies. I waited for him at SLU, specifically at the nearby computer shops there since he was playing. Once I saw him, we made the transaction and ended fast. I obtained P70.</p><p>I went home and continued the day as normal. Next up: Ecko Ultd. polo tomorrow.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-02-19',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'A Losing Streak with Extra Change',
            'description' => '<p>Midterm exams starts today. First up: Multimedia Systems. We took the exam on lecture period at our lab room in M307. There were still some who came late so they were given a -10 deduction to their exam score XD. I got 74/100. Not bad!</p><p>I went home to play 2 ranked games in LOL. I used Teemo and won those 2 matches with a record of 14-3 and 19-3. Afterwards, I reviewed Chapters 6 and 7 Exam answers on the internet (we won\'t be having the CCNA 2 exam today yet). I got out of the house and took my lunch at Bibac before my SAD class. Yeah, I\'m amazed that sir only put 3 questions on the exam. The 3rd question was an application of what we learned (I hardly learned anything!). Anyway, I got 26/50 for the first 2 questions (the 3rd wasn\'t added yet). I did better than Prelims!</p><p>Nothing much for CCNA 2. Took the last 2 chapter exams for Midterms and went home. I paid P20 and received my change. When I got off the jeep, I realized I got the wrong change. At first I thought I got P13 (all one-peso coins) until I counted it and it totalled to P43.25! It was too late to give it back. My bad.</p><p>It was useless playing LOL after reaching home. The 7 games were all losses! Worst, they blamed me for feeding! At least I don\'t surrender from a match (I\'m not a sissy to easily back down from a fight, unlike some players out there).</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 19, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-03-16',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Kamile\'s Drunken Night Fiasco',
            'description' => '<p>Finally, it\'s Friday! Time flies so fast that in the next 2 weeks, it\'ll be April. I woke up late today, missing my Multimedia Systems lab class at 8:55 AM. To curb that up, I finished my Systems Analysis and Design project instead before we pass it later in class at 2:35 PM. It was actually rushed since I lacked time (plus I did most of the project paper\'s content). Groupmates aren\'t cooperative enough. Besides, I need to pass whatever we finished since I\'m on the brink of failing Systems Analysis and Design (no wonder it has an acronym of SAD).</p><p>I went to Lemonet to play LOL (got nagged by Reyn haha!). I didn\'t make a bad choice after all. We won 5 consecutive ranked games! Because of that, I made it in the promotion series. She finished her series and was promoted to Silver II. Out of the blue, Kamile texted me if I want to join them at The Ampersand later in the evening. Without hesitation, I agreed (besides I\'m still in town and haven\'t went home yet). Then I left Lemonet.</p><p>Kamile told me to head to Zola and chill for awhile. They were seated at the middle. Kamile was wearing that Cara Delevigne shirt that I gave her last Christmas. Ange was here too. They had 2 bottles of San Mig Light, sharing the drinks together. After awhile, we headed to The Ampersand to meet Kamile\'s older sister and their friend. I paid for our taxi fare and in turn, she treated me our entrance fee. Now that\'s fair and square! We deposited our bags to the storage clerk before heading upstairs to The Ampersand.</p><p>Inside, there were still few people around. We\'re actually too early! We had 3 different cocktail towers for the 10 of us, varying in colors of orange, blue and white XD. I only knew Kamile, Ange and Mike personally (Kamile\'s older sister, Ate Karissa, and I are only mere acquaintances). All the rest are strangers to me.</p><p>On our 4th cocktail round (blue-colored cocktail on its 2nd round and the other 2 still on their 1st round), I\'ve been noticing that Kamile is going to the CR a couple of times (5 times since we entered). So I began to worry and asked her friends on her whereabouts. They said they don\'t know. Then I received a text from her that reads "Di kug bs kya dto kuh tablr lpit cr". Oh, she\'s drunk! I immediately headed out and found her sitting (in a bent position) by the VIP bench closest to the CR. I comforted her and she handed her Iphone to me and puked on the black carpet. It was the 1st time I saw her really drunk.</p><p>Ange found us both and told me to grab our bags already. I offered to carry Kamile but Ange refused. I got our bags and as I turned around, Ate Karissa and her chubby friend showed up (they were also MIA too). We let Kamile relax before I hailed a cab for them. To my surprise, I realized I forgot to give her phone back. Me and Mike were the only ones left. He said he knows where she lives, not too far from The Camp. We decided to walk it up.</p><p>She lives at St. Joseph Village (the opposite intersection going to Berkeley school). They have a bungalow-type house. Once there, we waited for around 30 minutes for Ange to come out. Then we gave the phone and left the premises. I took note of their house number: #18 or #22 (I don\'t know which because they\'re both placed on the gate). Tomorrow is CEA Night! XD</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 20, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-03-20',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Passing a Subject to Reward Myself By Playing Games',
            'description' => '<p>Today is the 2nd day of the Final exams. Just like the previous trimesters, the Finals exams schedule is a mess. Tomorrow is Friday and it is scheduled as a TThS day. This means that we have a regular class meeting on TThS subjects. We took our IT Presentation Skills exam today though. I got 34/62</p><p>Our Systems Analysis and Design presentation is scheduled at 2:35 PM. I sacrificed my CCNA 2 lab class just so we can end this S-A-D agony once and for all. Sir Dilan asked questions and among his feedbacks, the DFDs still had a lot of violations. That\'s what I should really improve on. I saw my grades at Sir Dilan\'s laptop. Surprisingly, I passed! He graded our presentation. My grades were 73-74-77, in order. Ironically, Ric passed but Christian failed. I was surprised because I was expecting he would pass but he didn\'t. Seriously though, I nearly cried when I knew I passed! This awesome feeling!</p><p>To get this weird excitement off my chest, I played LOL at Lemonet. 1 ranked duo game each with Reyn and Kuya Alfie with a lose and won match, respectively. After that, I went home and played Dying Light in the PS4. It\'s my 3rd day of playing it because I enjoyed this fantastic zombie-survival game so much! Daddy made an excellent suggestion, no doubt.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 20, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-04-16',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 4,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'LOVELESS',
            'description' => '<p>An excerpt from the video game "Crisis Core: Final Fantasy VII" where the main antagonist, Genesis, always recites this.</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">PROLOGUE</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">When the war of the beasts brings about the world\'s end,</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The goddess descends from the sky</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Wings of light and dark spread afar</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">She guides us to bliss, her gift everlasting</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">ACT I</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Infinite in mystery is the gift of the goddess</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We seek it thus and take to the sky</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Ripples form on the water\'s surface</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The wandering soul knows no rest</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">ACT II</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">There is no hate, only joy</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">For you are beloved by the goddess</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hero of the dawn, healer of worlds</p>
                <hr />
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Dreams of the morrow hath the shattered soul</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Pride is lost</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Wings stripped away, the end is nigh</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">ACT III</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">My friend, do you fly away now?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">To a world that abhors you and I?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">All that awaits you is a somber morrow</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">No matter where the winds may blow</p>
                <hr />
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">My friend, your desire</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Is the bringer of life, the gift of the goddess</p>
                <hr />
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Even if the morrow is barren of promises,</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nothing shall forestall my return</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">ACT IV</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">My friend, the fates are cruel</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">There are no dreams, no honor remains</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The arrow has left the bow of the goddess</p>
                <hr />
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">My soul, corrupted by vengeance</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hath endured torment, to find the end of the journey</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">In my own salvation and your eternal slumber</p>
                <hr />
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Legend shall speak</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Of sacrifice at world\'s end</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The wind sails over the water\'s surface</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Quietly, but surely</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">ACT V</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Even if the morrow is barren of promises,</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nothing shall forestall my return</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">To become the dew that quenches the land</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">To spare the sands, the seas, the skies,</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I offer thee this silent sacrifice</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 21, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-05-31',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 4,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'The Chaos',
            'description' => '<p>By: Gerard Nolst Trenite (1922)</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">I.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Dearest creature in creation</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Study English pronunciation</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I will teach you in my verse</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sounds like corpse, corps, horse and worse</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">II.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I will keep you, Suzy, busy</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Make your head with heat grow dizzy</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Tear in eye, your dress will tear</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">So shall I! Oh hear my prayer</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">III.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Just compare heart, beard and heard</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Dies and diet, lord and word</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sword and sward, retain and Britain</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Mind the latter, how it\'s written</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Now I surely will not plague you</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">With such words as plaque and ague</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">But be careful how you speak</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Say break and steak, but bleak and streak</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">V.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Cloven, oven, how and low</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Script, receipt, show, poem and toe</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hear me say, devoid of trickery</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Daughter, laughter and <a href="#the-chaos-ref-1"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Terpsichore</span><sup>1</sup></a></p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;"></p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">VI.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Typhoid, measles, topsails, aisles</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Exiles, similes and reviles</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Scholar, vicar and cigar</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Solar, mica, war and far</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">VII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">One, anemone, Balmoral</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Kitchen, lichen, laundry, laurel</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Gertrude, German, wind and mind</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Scene, <a href="#the-chaos-ref-2"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Melpomene</span><sup>2</sup></a>, mankind</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">VIII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Billet does not rhyme with ballet</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Bouquet, wallet, mallet, chalet</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Blood and flood are not like food</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nor is mould like should and would</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IX.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Viscous, viscount, load and broad</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Toward, to forward, to reward</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">And your pronunciation\'s OK</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">When you correctly say croquet</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">X.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Rounded, wounded, grieve and sieve</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Friend and fiend, alive and live</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Ivy, privy, famous, clamour</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">And enamour rhyme with hammer</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;"></p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XI.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">River, rival, tomb, bomb, comb</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Doll and roll and some and home</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Stranger does not rhyme with anger</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Neither does devour with clangour</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Souls but foul, haunt but aunt</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Font, front, won\'t, want, grand and grant</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Shoes, goes, does. Now first say finger,</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">And then singer, ginger, linger</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XIII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Real, zeal, mauve, gauze, gouge, and gauge</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Marriage, foliage, mirage and age</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Query does not rhyme with very</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nor does fury sound like bury</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XIV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Dost, lost, post and doth, cloth, loth</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Job, nob, bosom, transom, oath</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Though the differences seem little,</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We say actual but victual</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Refer does not rhyme with deafer</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Feoffer does and zephyr, heifer</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Mint, pint, senate and sedate</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Dull, bull, and George ate late</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XVI.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Scenic, Arabic, Pacific</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Science, conscience, scientific</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Liberty, library, heave and heaven</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Rachel, ache, moustache, eleven</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XVII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We say hallowed but allowed</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">People, leopard, towed but vowed</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Mark the differences, moreover</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Between mover, cover, clover</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XVIII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Leeches, breeches, wise, precise</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Chalice, but police and lice</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Camel, constable, unstable</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Principle, disciple, label</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XIX.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Petal, panel and canal</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Wait, surprise, plait, promise, pal</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Worm and storm, chaise, chaos, chair</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Senator, spectator, mayor</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XX.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Tour but our and succour, four</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Gas, alas and Arkansas</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sea, idea, Korea, area</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Psalm, Maria but malaria</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;"></p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXI.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Youth, south, southern, cleanse and clean</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Doctrine, turpentine, marine</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Compare alien with Italian</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Dandelion and battalion</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sally with ally, yea, ye</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Eye, I, ay, aye, whey and key</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Say aver but ever, fever</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Neither, leisure, skein, deceiver</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXIII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;"><a href="#the-chaos-ref-3"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Heron</span><sup>3</sup></a>, granary, canary</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Crevice and device and aerie</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Face but preface, not efface</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Phlegm, phlegmatic, ass, glass, bass</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXIV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Large but target, gin, give, verging</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Ought, out, joust and scour, scourging</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Ear but earn and wear and tear</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Do not rhyme with here but ere</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Seven is right but so is even</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hyphen, roughen, nephew Stephen</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Monkey, donkey, Turk and jerk</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Ask, grasp, wasp and cork and work</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;"></p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXVI.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Pronunciation, think of Psyche!</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Is a paling stout and spikey?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Won\'t it make you lose your wits</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Writing groats and saying grits?</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXVII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">It\'s a dark abyss or tunnel</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Strewn with stones, stowed, solace, gunwale</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Islington and Isle of Wight</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Housewife, verdict, indict</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">XXVIII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Finally, which rhymes with enough?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Though, through, plough or dough or cough?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hiccough has the sound of cup</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">My advice is to give up!</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a id="the-chaos-ref-1"></a><sup>1</sup> - means "delight in dancing" was one of the nine Muses and goddess of dance and chorus in Greek Mythology.</li>
                <li><a id="the-chaos-ref-2"></a><sup>2</sup> - In Greek Mythology, she is initially the Muse of Singing, she then became the Muse of Tragedy, for which she is best known now.</li>
                <li><a id="the-chaos-ref-3"></a><sup>3</sup> - also known as "Hero of Alexandria", he is a Greek mathematician and engineer who was active in his native city of Alexandria, Roman Egypt.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>This is a classic English poem containing about 800 of the worst irregularities in English spelling and pronunciation. This is the first known version containing 146 lines.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 22, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2014-05-24',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 4,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'The Golden Sun',
            'description' => '<p>By: Jenica Cayabyab and Tristan Pullido</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">I.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The golden sun gently peeps</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Among the green towering mountains</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">As its rays reflect and slowly leaps</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">On mother nature who had just awaken</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">II.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The birds sing such sweet music</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">While trees dance in a cheerful song</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">And the waves collide really quick</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">That they run back to the peaceful horizon</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">III.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">One could close his eyes to be welcomed again</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">By a paradise as perfect as Eden</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">No one would have thought this will be by then</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Of man\'s technologies, a dumpsite not garden</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Buildings made on flattened mountains</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Vehicles eat on energy below</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Blue skies filled with gray stains</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Gray air, dirty to everyone, a no-no</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">V.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The plastics that harm the smallest lands</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Chemicals that kill these young, little plants</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">All from man\'s curious but deadly hands</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The product of all our selfish wants</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">VI.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Aren\'t we one of God\'s creations</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Along with nature, earth and everything?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We weren\'t made to bring divisions</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We were born to take care of all God\'s beings</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">VII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We were happy, everyone was</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Simply by just wandering inside nature</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Simply by lying down the thick, green grass</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Simply by living without destroying pastures</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">VIII.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Yes, indeed, many of us have been in cases</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Strived to bring back what nature was before</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The rest needs reality to crash to their faces</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Before nature actually shuts its long-opened door</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 30, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2011-10-17',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 4,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Salvation',
            'description' => '<p>By: Troy Mascenon and Ida Caja</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">I.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Our world is a beautiful place you see</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Man and nature living in harmony</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Breath-taking wonders and heart-racing views</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">That fills you with joy and makes you feel new</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">II.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The clouds so fluffy, the sky so smooth</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The light that guides you in every move</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The trees so sturdy, the winds so fresh</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Thanks God, you\'re the best!</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">III.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">And God says "Anything for you"</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I wonder how I can see God in full view</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I pinch myself, no this isn\'t a dream</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I\'m in heaven now, that\'s what it seems</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">God showed the world that I used to live in</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Full of greed, full of wrath, full of sin</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The air is filled with smoke, darkness fills the air</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The water is polluted, life is hard to bear</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">V.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">"This is all your fault" God exclaimed out loud</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">"You took everything for granted, brought yourselves down"</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">"But I love you, I\'ll keep you safe and warm"</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">"No matter what faults, I\'ll take you away from harm"</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 30, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2011-10-17',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 4,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'The Big Difference',
            'description' => '<p>By: Sharmaine Modgil and Kristine Prieto</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">I.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I remember the cold breeze</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">When it brushed my hair with ease</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">As I sat under an old tree</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">But now, what do I see?</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">II.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Now, what can I say?</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">As I wake up day by day</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">This feeling I have is strange</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Now that everything has changed</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">III.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I used to watch the sun as it sets</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Now, I\'m simply filled with regrets</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I remember the waves crash so gently</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">But now, everything\'s depleting silently</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I missed the high mountains I climbed</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">On the peak, joy is what I find</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The sound of the waterfalls I used to hear</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">But now, the end is almost near</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">V.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Now I see the big difference</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Only if we all come to our sense</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We must start the change now</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">We must find a way how</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('April 30, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
