        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'A Night at Singgles Bar',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s the last Friday of the month. I decided to go out to SM and check the schedule for Avengers: Age of Ultron. I texted Kendrick and Kamile to invite them to watch the movie with me. Neither one replied. After checking the schedule, I realized all cinemas (except Cinema 4, it was Fast and Furious 7 movie being shown in there) were showing Avengers: Age of Ultron. It was just released a couple of days ago.</p><p>It\'s nearly 2 PM and I need to eat. So I ate at Sawrapped nearby. I ordered one of my favorite meals: Sisig! My order also included a regular iced tea and 2 extra rice. So delicious! The order amounted to P346 but it\'s worth it anyway.</p><p>Afterwards, Norina texted me to go out drinking with her at Singgles Bar. At first, I didn\'t know where it is. Then she described it where. It\'s located at Lower Session Road, beside Yellow Cab. I thought she\'s already there, so I hurriedly walked down Session Road. When I got to the destination, I realized she\'s still on her way there (I\'m always early). By 3:24 PM, she finally arrived! Last time we drank together was on December 6, 2013. Been a long time!</p><p>She went up first. When I saw the bar\'s entrance, I was able to remember a time where she invited me here before. I realized it\'s the 2nd time she invited me here. She decided that we sit at the counter. She ordered 2 Blue Lagoon cocktails worth P180 each, Chicken Fillet worth P130 and I ordered 2 Red Horse Stallion beers (which was eventually cancelled). Then we started the conversation (we had not went out drinking for a long time) as we drink the cocktail. I sang "Upside Down", "Kung Kailangan Mo Ako", "Untitled" and "When You Say Nothing At All". Norina sang "Hanggang Ngayon" and "How To Love".</p><p>We finished the Blue Lagoon cocktails and she ordered a case of Emperador Lights (the replacement for the Red Horse beers). During the conversation, she saw a small cockroach on the Chicken Fillet and reported it to one of the ladies in the bar. They got that plate and gave our bill as well. To my surprise, she treated our drinks (I thought she totally forgot about it since December 6, 2013). We were asked to transfer to a table because the lady feared the cockroach will come back haha! They gave another Chicken Fillet as a replacement to the 1st one (no additional charges yey!).</p><p>Then came Karla, Norina\'s friend. The bulk of our conversations was really about Norina\'s boyfriend. Surprisingly, her boyfriend followed us there. This is already the signal that we needed to go because her boyfriend is "jealous" of me, according to Norina. I don\'t know what is to be jealous about haha! So we parted ways. Me and Karla headed up north while the 2 of them hailed a cab there at Yellow Cab. My convos with Norina will truly be unforgettable, as well as the moment spent.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 8, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-04-24',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Labor Day 2015',
            'description' => '<p>Today is a holiday: Labor Day. It\'s a day dedicated to employees to take a day off their office seats and relax for a while. I have scheduled this day to have my haircut since my hair is getting itchy. Afterwards, I went to SM to check the schedule of Avengers: Age of Ultron once again. Line is full so I didn\'t buy a ticket. QBox Station is my next destination. I purchased their card so I can use it every time I go there. The QBox Station card is worth P20 only.</p><p>I played there for the 1st time and my 1st game is WWE 2K15. The console on my station is XBox One, which is also my 1st time to use it. So lucky! My very 1st match on the game is HBK vs HHH on 2K Showcase Mode. I had a hard time beating HHH since I was alienated with XBox\'s controls. I had 3 attempts before giving up (I used most of my 1st 30 minutes just for 1 match). When my station turned off automatically (signifying my time is up), I extended for 1 hour. This time, I toyed around with my favorite mode of the series: WWE Universe Mode. P60 for 30 minutes and P120 for 1 hour seems expensive to me but playing one of my favorite video game series is worth it.</p><p>At home, Daddy, Tita Jhan, Lois and Patrick left for Manila at around 11 PM. I\'m left home alone. I want to commute alone in going to Manila but an outing with Ate Kamille for a kart experience is better.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 8, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-05-01',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Pampanga Escapade',
            'description' => '<p>We made it to Ate Kamille\'s house here in Pampanga last night. Before that, we rode a van designated for Dagupan to check on Ate Collen and along with their friend, we had a spectacular view of the seaside somewhere in Bonuan. Then me and Ate Kamille headed for Tarlac to have the long-planned karting. Sadly, it rained hard and karting is unavailable due to the wet tracks. Well, that sucks. So we just went to Pampanga.</p><p>I\'ve never been here ever. Before heading to their house, Ate Kamille showed me where "The Walking Street" is. At least now I know why there are a lot of foreigners in here. Hahaha! Then she showed me where the original Sisig was made. It\'s an ordinary carinderia owned by "Aling Lucing", who invented the legendary Sisig meal. Sadly, she passed away. The store is just a few blocks from Ate Kamille\'s house (they also own a sari-sari store).</p><p>We woke up in time for lunch. It\'s not that hot here in Pampanga thankfully. We went to Robinsons Angeles to play at Tom\'s World. It\'s like Quantum but tokens cost P4 instead of P6. Ate Kamille nearly lost her phone inside the premises. We were asking around if they found a phone. I still had to text Ate Collen to inform her about it and before I could send the message, an honest kid in green shirt approached her and handed the phone. It fell on the seat she was at. She said she nearly had a "heart attack" because she felt so scared on what transpired. She thanked his dad and his siblings for having such an honest son. She bought tokens to give it to the kid but sadly, they left.</p><p>Ate Kamille still have 2 tokens left. We transferred to the other Tom\'s World of the mall. There were more people out there. We played ice hockey. I lost to her at the score of 1-2. Afterwards, we went home as our next stop is on the gym.</p><p>The gym is Shoulders &amp; Boulders. The walk-in fee is P35 but only paid P20 (Ate Kamille shouldered the P15 so she would pay P50 instead). Cardio exercise for 15-25 minutes then strength exercises and lastly, ab exercises before leaving. I felt some "gym rust" since it\'s been awhile I get to use the equipments.</p><p>The Pampanga escapade, as I call it, didn\'t stop there. We took a short rest at home then went to SM Clark. I get to watch Avengers: Age of Ultron finally! The best scene was when Ultron\'s army attacked the Avengers. They\'re just on an empty ruin fending themselves. After watching, we rode a jeep going to Didi\'s Pizza. We ordered the Combination Pizza, where cheese, salami, mushroom, pepperoni and sausage toppings are all in 1 pizza. So delicious! Our last stop is at a bar just across the street. Inside, the place is so beautiful! There was a live band, who is on their last set. The girls wore super shorts and their legs whiter than the searchlight. Hahaha!</p><p>Finally, we went home. We\'re going back to Baguio tomorrow as well. The karting will probably happen soon. We\'re just unlucky that the bad weather occurred on the day of the outing.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 8, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-05-05',
        ]);

