            'date_published' => '2015-08-07',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #6',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Constipation"</p><p>On June 3, 2015, I thought it would be a normal day but it wasn\'t. I went home having this nauseous feeling so I went to the C.R. to <a href="#constipation-ref-1"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">take a dump</span><sup>1</sup></a>. To my surprise, I had a hard time losing bowel movement and was reeling in pain. It took me more than 30 minutes to finish. This could have been Sawrapped\'s fault because I ordered Sisig for lunch and it wasn\'t that delicious (how could Sisig do this to me?). I had stomach aches yet I still finished my meal for I hate leaving leftover foods.</p><p>Eventually, I had my dinner and told Noel of this nauseous feeling and he suggested that I drink hot water to lessen the pain. So I went to take a dump again and I don\'t think it worked. I screeched in agony and shouted like a beast because of the excruciating pain. Each time I try to move from my position, the pain goes to its threshold. Just imagine yourself burning in a whim, your life is depleting so fast that you just want to give up. Luckily, I stood brave to continue fighting because I had trust in myself.</p><p>This nauseous feeling had to continue until the end of the week. Each time I finish dealing with this agony, my butt feels hot and sensitive. It\'s like you just recovered from surgery and moving less reduces pain. It was like hell literally. When the agony is over, it is exiting from hell. Because of this, I had to research about it. It turned out to be <a href="#constipation-ref-2"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">constipation</span><sup>2</sup></a>. It had something to do with "lack of fluids", preferably water. Since then, I\'ve been drinking more water, as a lesson for experiencing <a href="#constipation-ref-3"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">dehydration</span><sup>3</sup></a> last month.</p><p>After 8 days, I believed I recovered from this stressful experience. As much as I hate to say this but I\'m not eating at Sawrapped at this moment (this isn\'t goodbye yet, Sisig). Until then, prevention is the best cure. Hopefully, I don\'t experience this ever again. The best thing among all these is that it was a self-medication process and never informed anyone but Noel about this. 3 pieces of Dulcolax soothed the agonizing pain.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a id="constipation-ref-1"></a><sup>1</sup> - an idiomatic expression meaning "to lose bowel movement" aka LBM.</li>
                <li><a id="constipation-ref-2"></a><sup>2</sup> - a disorder where the individual experiences difficulty in losing bowel movement, feeling pain each time he tries to remove waste. Waste being expelled is very small and dry.</li>
                <li><a id="constipation-ref-3"></a><sup>3</sup> - related to constipation but the waste being expelled in the body is watery and slimy. Stomach ache is much painful.</li>
            </ul>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 10, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-06-12',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Taking Independence Day a Little Too Literally',
            'description' => '<p>We\'re a day removed from yesterday\'s National Independence Day. Today is a Saturday and I have no class today. I decided to go watch a movie in SM. The movie happened to be San Andreas starring Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson.</p><p>I arrived at SM in time to check the schedule. I realized it\'s the final showing of the movie at 3:40 PM. I bought a ticket and waited for an hour to watch the movie since I got a little late. To make up for time lost, I roamed around the mall. I checked out Comic Alley, a new store, to check some anime merchandise. Ryzher told me that he bought a Teemo hat and Rammus hat there. That got me very curious. I really did saw it but I decided not to buy it. Instead, I bought a Final Fantasy keychain resembling Lightning\'s sword for P129.</p><p>After waiting for that long, it\'s time to get inside the cinema. The movie is showing at Cinema 1 and I watched the movie alone. This is the 2nd time I\'m watching a movie all by myself (the 1st one was Insurgent). I got no worries. Anyway, I enjoyed it very much. If only there\'s someone who would accompany me, then I would have been so happy.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 10, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-06-13',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'A Kazia Night',
            'description' => '<p>A rainy Saturday greets my cold morning. I have no classes every Saturdays but I\'ll be going to school to wait for Kazia. I wore my very thick FUBU windbreaker due to an extremely cold weather. I arrived at school before 2 PM and she wasn\'t there yet. Gate 1 was the meeting place and I waited for around 30 minutes before she finally arrived. Anyway, she\'s one of the few friends who\'s worth waiting for.</p><p>We went to Zentea and it was our first time there. She treated me. I ordered "Carnival" (caramel milk tea) while Kazia ordered "Altitude" (almond milk tea). She required my assistance on building a business website for one of her subjects. There were 2 options: Wordpress and Joomla. We opted for the 1st one since I happen to have a website using that site. The milk teas were large as they are worth P75 each. Our conversations mostly consist on Kazia getting acquainted with Wordpress. I apologized at certain points where I couldn\'t answer her queries. Anyway, she\'s a fast learner and very independent.</p><p>Next up: SM Baguio. I invited her to watch the Minions movie, in which she was hesitant at first. It never pushed through because we had to wait for another hour. So we went to Red Green Peppers to eat but she refused to eat with me since she\'s not hungry. I ordered Grilled Chicken Burrito Bowl and an extra rice. Then I accompanied her home, carrying the laptop for her. She lives in Cabinet Hill. Feels good to help someone out. Finally, I had my haircut near Kumon to end my day.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 10, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-07-18',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Top of the Class and Earned P1,000',
            'description' => '<p>We\'re nearly closing the month of July. In 9 days, we\'re entering August. August is the month where surprises start. This day is far from excitement. Last night, a customer confirmed he will indeed buy my 4 clothes that I\'m selling. He inquired last week but it had to be delayed because I had my Tribal and Pelle Pelle shirts laundried. After receiving the laundry last night, the deal shall push through.</p><p>Before that, I need to attend my classes first. The meetup time is between 10:50 - 3:50 PM and he\'ll just text me on the time we\'ll meet. In school, I got the highest grade on CCNA 3 with 93. I\'m so happy! I went home happy. I waited for the buyer\'s go signal as I prepare the 4 items he will buy: Ecko jacket, RRJ shirt, Tribal shirt and Pelle Pelle shirt. The items cost P450, P150, P200 and P200, respectively. They summed up to a whopping P1,000!</p><p>I immediately went to SM for the meetup venue. Wearing my Ecko jacket on a sunny day feels so awkward but I have to. Anyways, I waited for him on Baguio Bingo. He didn\'t take long and the transaction was fast. Thank God he answered my prayers!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 10, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-07-23',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #7',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"The Book Thrower"</p><p>In 2010, my 3rd year high school tenure was the worst year of my HS life. It was the loneliest, most outcasted year ever. Seriously, 2009 was a damn happy year. Everything suddenly changed. That year, I had a good time. Then in 2010, I had problems with Koreans. Not only do I despise the smell of <a href="#the-book-thrower-ref-1"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Kimchi</span><sup>1</sup></a>, I despise their behaviors too. They were the noisy type. Koreans have loud mouths because they talk very fast.</p><p>Before the semestral break in October, I stole her <a href="#the-book-thrower-ref-2"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">electric dictionary</span><sup>2</sup></a>. One day, during lunch break, me and Ryzher decided to play a prank on Melisa, owner of the dictionary. We had a sack inside the classroom then (I forgot why). I told him to place it inside the sack because hiding the dictionary behind the books in the bookshelf could be easily spotted. Dismissal came and Melisa already noticed it was missing. Teacher Vic (our adviser) ordered to remove every contents of our bags but no one has it. It was only me and Ryzher left and we got the dictionary from the sack. Ryzher told me to have it and suggested to sell it (but never did so). I hid it on the 2nd house in Patrick\'s old, vandalized cabinet. It was hidden and never heard of ever since. The dictionary has since been forgotten.</p><p>In 2011, I transferred to Northridge Academy, Inc. I had a successful tenure, becoming the batch\'s Prom King and honorable mention. After some time, Ryzher met up with me and asked him if our classmates knew about the book throwing incident and he said yes. Paolo told the story about it. It didn\'t matter anymore. The next year, I saw her studying in UC. One day, I decided to buy her a Kirby stuff toy in Blue Magic at SM and some chocolates to bury the hatchet between us. That was the last time we talked to each other. Hope I could see her again.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a id="the-book-thrower-ref-1"></a><sup>1</sup> - Koreans\' native food.</li>
                <li><a id="the-book-thrower-ref-2"></a><sup>2</sup> - a device used by Koreans with English translations to help them cope up in class.</li>
            </ul>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 17, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-08-17',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Dyed Hair And Staying Awake for 22 Hours',
            'description' => '<p>Today, Ate Collen dyed my hair brownish in color. She and Ate Kamille had recently dyed their hairs and they wanted to have my hair dyed as well. There was still some leftovers and they decided to use it on me. I feel hesitant at first and eventually, I convinced myself. I never had fully dyed my hair before (just some highlights 4 years ago). Today marks another milestone.</p><p>After dying my hair, we wanted to chill together. Patrick is still sleeping. We would play Monopoly if only he\'s awake. He was sleeping the whole day! We just played "PANTS" and "Hangman". A pen and paper is all we have. Today also marks the longest time stayed awake. From 6 AM to 4:15 AM, I\'m awake for around 22 hours! That\'s the record for 2015.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 20, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-08-11',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Tibayan Family Reunion 2015',
            'description' => '<p>Wow! Today is one, big family reunion! Tito Marlo and his family came here from USA. Those kids are too fluent with English. Tito Perry and company followed. Kuya Macky joins in as well. They came and arrived in the morning. Tonight, it will be Tita Gemma and her family coming as well. Tito Wilson and family will never miss out as well. Lastly, Tita Vina and Tito Jimmy came back from the farm. Wow, we\'re one, small tribe already. Mama missed out on the fun, if only she was here.</p><p>Tatay and my other uncles stayed outside drinking Emperador Light. Others stayed inside. Me and my cousins had our own table as well. We drank 2 cases of Red Horse beers. The fun didn\'t stop there! We went to Jheric\'s house to eat. Oh yeah, there was lots of foods there. Tacos, chickens and nachos are in the table. Those tacos are so delicious! I keep on getting it. In fact, after a short dinner there, we got some tacos (there\'s lots of it anyway). We went home with 3 paper plates filled with tacos! Tita Vina and Tita Carol were even surprised about it. Then the fun continues.</p><p>It\'s 3 AM and I\'m tired already. Most of us enjoyed the "get together" and slept with ease. I hope it happens again.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 20, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-08-15',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'First Stint at Driving a Vehicle',
            'description' => '<p>Happy 43rd birthday to Mama and Mama Cathy! To show my small appreciation for the things they\'ve done, I bought a bouquet of roses and 2 boxes of Ferrero Rocher chocolates at SM worth P199.75 each. I did it after my classes. The strong rain didn\'t hinder me from buying the gifts. I was able to send the photos of the gifts to Mama in Viber so she could see the gifts even if she\'s not physically here. Then she called and I greeted her. While I was talking to her, tears ran down my face as I couldn\'t tell her how guilty I am for not taking care of the house. Then I left.</p><p>I hailed a taxi going to 50\'s Diner in Leonard Wood Rd. but mistakenly ended up at the Military Cut-off branch. Ate Kamille fetched me using Mama Cathy\'s car. She finally taught me how to drive! She has been planning to teach me for the past years and tonight, I had my opportunity. I practiced accelerating and turning around as well as starting the car and setting the car to Park mode. We did this at South Drive Rd. After the short yet unforgettable experience, we drove to the Pitstop bar to meet Patrick, Kuya Macky and Kuya Brian who all started drinking beers ahead of us. We just ordered 1 bucket of San Mig Light and Red Horse beers, then we left.</p><p>Next stop: Night Market. It\'s only 11 PM and there\'s still a lot of people strolling around. We didn\'t buy any clothes though, just had street foods. I didn\'t eat with them though. While they were taking a break, I am still sad over my guilt and shame on Mama\'s birthday. I had to cut our conversation short because my cousins are yelling and getting mad at me for still staying at home awhile ago. If only they understood how it feels like greeting your own mother on the best day of their life, then they wouldn\'t be putting me at pressure. The short conversation still meant so much to me.</p><p>Before going home, we fetched Rachel at her unit in Ina Mansion just near Burnharm Park. She was able to stay at our house temporarily, had chit-chats and brought her back to her unit. They ended the night happily. As for me, I had mixed emotions. Happiness for being taught how to drive for the first time. Sadness for not having a lengthy conversation with Mama. What can I do? My cousins are sometimes egotistic and selfish.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 20, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-09-08',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'First Stint Inside a Cave',
            'description' => '<p>Phew! Just arrived home from last night\'s camping at Jackson\'s resort in Camp 3 Kennon Road. It was my first time making a bonfire using driftwoods plus wooden cardboards. Me and Jackson\'s collegemates in CBA slept in a mini-cave overlooking a river below it. Before reaching the mini-cave, we had to cross a long footbridge that night. Just imagine how dark it was.</p><p>The next morning, we had Adobo for breakfast. Rovelyn teased me when she called me a "loner". It hurted me so much that for the rest of the morning, I was literally quiet! She thinks I have a happy life but it\'s not. So by around 10 AM, Jackson wants us to experience the caves. A long walk from our mini-cave ensued. The cave\'s entrance is extremely ridiculous. We need to crawl to get inside. Wow, it\'s my 1st experience to go inside an actual cave. So many obstacles. I nearly fell off a huge rock yet luckily, I had good balance. Our flashlights were about to run out so we travelled back to the entrance. We\'re thankful we got out alive (and saw the glimmering sun). We reached halfway to the 1st exit before going back. Spooky yet thrilling adventure.</p><p>Before going home to Camp 8, we took a dip in the resort\'s very cold pool. I was chilling the whole time. Then Jackson\'s collegemates went ahead and soon we followed as well. Thank God I survived that cave!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('December 28, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-10-04',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'LAN Battle: Team Lemonet vs Team Koreans',
            'description' => '<p>I\'ve been seeing Bessy manning the mini-canteen at the Nursing Building\'s 5th floor frequently. I bought 2 Kopiko 78 degrees beverage at the mini-canteen at different times wherein she was the one who assisted me. I don\'t think she remembers me at all even if she lives at our compound. She doesn\'t go out very often.</p><p>I went to Lemonet after my Software Engineering class. Ken is manning the shop. Since there\'s no customers leaving their seats yet, we had a coffee break at Calliope. Our favorite bar girl named Michelle served our coffees. These are unlimited brewed coffees and milk is the only thing they charge. So after we had 2 rounds of coffee (worth P55), we went back to the shop. Oh look! We were challenged by the Koreans for a 5v5 custom match at the shop. We accepted.</p><p>We picked our best roles in LOL. As always, I am the team\'s ADR, using Caitlyn. Zedrick picked Ziggs, Jics picked Olaf, Chibi picked Morgana and her brother picked Zed. At the heat of battle, my team communicated in Filipino, going as far as translating every English word to Filipino so the Koreans won\'t understand. This is a friendly match though.</p><p>Team Lemonet won against the Koreans. It\'s a hard-fought battle and we came out victorious. Until next time.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('December 28, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-10-16',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Cat Operation: For Accompaniment Purposes',
            'description' => '<p>There ain\'t much on a Sunday. I decided to clean the house today. I started at the living room in the morning. Then my C.R. at noon. Lastly, the kitchen at night. Tiring yet worth it.</p><p>Out of boredom, I decided to lure the stray cats that are always wandering around. There is still a leftover Boneless Bangus on the refrigerator and I used it as a bait. Since there\'s 3 stray cats wandering in the garage, I only need 1 of them. I sliced the fish into bite-size pieces that the cats can chew on. I make sure that I don\'t scare them so I leave the food by the stairs and as much as possible, they must not see me or they\'ll be scared. I peep by the window and as they get closer to the main gate, I slowly sneaked to the front door to check if they have made it inside the house.</p><p>Eventually, all 3 stray cats made it. As they are eating the last pieces of the Bangus, I hurriedly went outside and immediately closed the gate. The small, black kitten was trapped while the 2 fled. I blocked its escape route by placing the brown chair by the gate. The cat could escape in the door handle if I wouldn\'t block it. This cat will "accompany" me through the night. Sorry, I needed an awesome companion in the house since I\'m alone.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('December 28, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-10-25',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Mama\'s Initial Homecoming After 2 Years',
            'description' => '<p>I\'m so excited that this is the day my mom would return home to the Philippines. She left for Australia last April 18, 2013 and it\'s been 2 years since I saw her. I did some last-minute cleaning of the house despite being allergic to dust. Yes, I persevered this condition and did my best to keep the house dust-free yet I know it\'s not enough. Certain areas like Mama\'s room isn\'t fully clean. Good to know that Ate Kamille helped clean the kitchen. It\'s pristine and neat! Living room is clean too.</p><p>We are bound to Manila using a rented van with tatay, Lola, Mama Cathy, Patrick and Noel. By 3 AM, we left Baguio. During the trip, I\'ve been sleeping very frequently. We went to Manila Cemetery by 8 AM to pay respect to Tatay\'s parents and his friend who are buried there. Afterwards, we went to Tita Tess\' house in Caloocan and had lunch there. I had 2 rounds of fruit salad because it was so delicious! Half of the afternoon was spent there. They joked of a certain bazaar of cheap goods where "mga gamit na ninanakaw ng mga bumbero" is and so we went there. Mama Cathy bought a flashlight from that weird bazaar.</p><p>After the trips we had for this day, we\'re finially going to fetch Mama. The sun has already set and we made it to NAIA. We persevered waiting for Mama at Terminal 2, as we constantly look at the screen because we are just very excited to see her. We ate at Jollibee to alleviate our hunger. Then we went to check the big screen again. The atmosphere in NAIA is really full of excitement and happiness as I was never been to an airport before. Everyone out there is waiting for their loved ones to steep foot in Philippine soil. Noel called my attention and told me he saw Mama already. I became more excited about it, especially Mama Cathy. Me, Patrick and Noel transferred to the taxi area and by 9:48 PM, Mama arrived! Wow, I\'ve never been so happy again when I saw her after 2 years! She carried 4 orange travelling bags with her in which she said that it\'s mostly food. Haha!</p><p>What a success! We went home immediately and has arrived Baguio by around 4 AM. Mama will stay here until January 11, 2016 where she\'ll go back to Australia once more. The good things is that she\'ll celebrate Christmas and New Year with us.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('December 28, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-11-20',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Starbucks Date with Classmates!',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s Bonifacio Day which means that there\'s no classes today! Yes! Today will be our Starbucks date with my friends. I\'ve been doing this annually every Christmas season for the past 2 years. Since December 2013, I\'ve enjoyed the company of my friends where it\'s my treat, as long as they come. Before that, I have a meet-up schedule in Shoppers\' Lane.</p><p>I bought a Teemo-quoted brown shirt which says "Never underestimate the power of the scout\'s code." that is actually a prize on win LOL LAN tournaments. Wow, I never realized it until I saw it on the website. It costs P300 and I got a free LOL baller (which resembles Garen\'s sword). We met up at 2:24 PM.</p><p>The Starbucks date is at 3 PM. Zel, Jules and Kevin will come. Kamile will follow. The meetup place is at JCO Donuts outside SM. Kevin arrived first followed by Jules and lastly Zel. Due to many people at the Starbucks in SM, we decided to have the date at their Session Road branch instead. All of us ordered Toffee Nut Latte except for Jules, who went for the Green Tea Latte.</p><p>Zel left first because she has work by 5 PM. Kevin accompanied her. Eventually Kamile showed up and abruptly left as well to get her White Planner Limited Edition in Starbucks SM. Afterwards, we parted ways.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('December 28, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-11-30',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => '24 Days Before Christmas 2015',
            'description' => '<p>Today is the 1st day of December. Wow, there\'s only 24 days left before Christmas. Session Road is closed today to celebrate and open the Christmas season here in Baguio. Tourists are coming to Baguio frequently to enjoy the cold climate.</p><p>Kamile texted me at 1:28 PM. I was just helping myself in fixing my room. Mama and Ate Anabel are fixing the mess outside. Kamile told me to go to Dairy Queen because Ate Karissa would treat me an ice cream of my choice (for helping them yesterday with the Starbucks Limited Edition White Planner). I chose a Cherry Strawberry Blizzard. Delicious!</p><p>By 5:15 PM, we watched the official opening of today\'s activity. UB\'s chorale team opened the festivities. By 5:30 PM, we both attender our classes. After my OS Applications class, I went back to Session Road for the Lantern Parade. Featuring the different school departments of SLU, the enormous displays of creativity marched down Session Road. Jordan accompanied me as we watched together.</p><p>After the Lantern Parade, I went home. Along the way, I saw Czha lining up the queue for the Mines View terminal. She\'s still pretty! I still have a crush on her even if she already have a boyfriend. Haha!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('December 28, 2015 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-12-01',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Mr. and Ms. UC Pageant Night',
            'description' => '<p>UC is special today. Tonight, it will have its annual Mr and Ms UC Pageant to be held at the gym between 6 PM to 9 PM. Alani, a close friend of mine, will represent us as Mr. CITCS while a 1st year student named Denielle will represent us as Ms. CITCS. After my OS Applications class, I checked how crowded the gym is. Lo and behold, it was indeed! The tickets are sold out and since I don\'t have one, I couldn\'t enter the gym. Roanne, my classmate in OS Applications, wanted to watch and she, too, has no ticket. Haha! We could only peep if there was a space, but there wasn\'t as well.</p><p>Luckily, Norina saved the day and treated me with 1 ticket. This leaves Roanne without a ticket. Then we saw Wilson exit the gym and treated Roanne with a ticket. This girl has a crush on me and she didn\'t even thanked me for getting her a ticket. What an ungrateful woman (sorry, I don\'t like you). Ugly face, ugly heart. Anyway, we went inside already.</p><p>We watched from the balcony because it\'s very crowded at the belchers. Alani didn\'t make it to Top 3 Mr UC. The runner-ups for Male were CTE (2nd) and JHS (1st). For Female, it was the same as in the Male category. Mr. UC was won by CCJE and Ms. UC to CON, who happens to be a foreigner. Alani won 1 award: Mr. Photogenic. The night was fantastic! Thanks to Norina and Wilson for the free tickets!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('January 2, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-12-05',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'An Extremely Rare Christmas With Parents And Brother',
            'description' => '<p>Daddy and Tita Jhan arrived in the wee hours of the morning. Thankfully, they\'ll celebrate Christmas with us. Today is very memorable. First, I played Crossfire after a 1-year hiatus with Noel and Aldrix at the computer shop not far from home. We battled 2 arrogant kids in a losing effort because of lag. It didn\'t matter, as I can beat them if it wasn\'t lag. Second, Mama dyed Patrick\'s, Daddy\'s and my hair to black (though there are shades of gray). I saw the sweetness between Mama and Daddy for a brief period when Mama is dying Daddy\'s hair. It\'s a moment that will hardly be replicated. Ever. Again.</p><p>Lastly, the most memorable of it all is having an unexpected family photo between the 4 of us. Seeing Mama and Daddy in 1 picture together brings me to happiness and sadness at the same time. My parents are already separated and witnessing them "together" just for a special occasion like Christmas is totally unforgettable. They made my Christmas very happy! Thank you to Ate Kamille for taking our Christmas family photo and to Tita Carol for that huge encouragement to get us a photo.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('January 2, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-12-24',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #8',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"My Pet"</p><p>On April 9, 2008, I celebrated my birthday at home. Among those who came to my birthday party were Bianca, Gian, Jayronn, Justin, Marisha, Ryzher and Shaira. Justin gave me a <a href="#my-pet-ref-1"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Bleach</span><sup>1</a></sup> figurine while Ryzher surprised me with a pet. He gave a hamster, complete with its cage and pet food. It was my very 1st pet to have. I named her as Roxanne because it was the "prettiest" name of a girl, in my opinion. Every night, I would feed her with that weird, smelly pet food Ryzher had provided. I took care of her for around a week and have to leave her to Mama because I\'m going to Manila to spend the rest of my vacation there.</p><p>When I came back to Baguio, I broke down in tears when I saw her cage at the garage. I knew it coming, she died. I was deeply saddened by Roxanne\'s loss, for I left her without my presence. Yet I moved on with it. If it was still alive, she would have grown bigger and would turn 8 years old on April 9, 2016.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a id="my-pet-ref-1"></a><sup>1</sup> - is a 2004 Japanese anime show. Though I never watched the show, it got me surprised as to why I got it as a gift.</li>
            </ul>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('January 2, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-01-01',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #9',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Chichi, the Stray Cat"</p><p>Since October 20, 2015, I\'ve started feeding a stray cat that\'s been wandering around our neighborhood for a couple of months now. She is a tri-colored cat: white as her most dominant color, orange on some spots of her body and gray on her head. I named her as <a href="#chichi-the-stray-cat-ref-1">Chichi<sup>1</sup></a> because I find the name very cute despite the cat being a wild animal. My fondness of cats made me want to help improve her life and so I decided to continue feeding her.</p><p>By January 6, 2016, people kept informing me that Chichi is pregnant. Ate Anabel kept asking me whether she\'s really pregnant or not. I declined. Then she asked me to question Kuya Brian about hearing cat meows on our house. He confirms it when he heard it from Patrick\'s room, specifically in his ceilings. By January 8, 2016, I was at Lola\'s veranda when I saw Chichi and her 2 kittens pass through an opening on our house roof. I believe this is where she probably gave birth. My suspicion of her being pregnant becomes more of a belief than a rumor when I noticed that she rarely sleeps in our stairs anymore when in fact she always sleeps there last year. I was surprised. By January 18, 2016, I started to let her inside the house. I want her to get used to it so that she\'ll never be frightened anymore. By January 23, 2016, Kuya Buckie and Ate Anabel informed me of a black kitten in our garage. Ironically, this is not Chichi\'s offspring as she ran away when I dropped the kitten to Chichi. In fact, before returning it to the garage, I carried it home, took a picture of it, then let it stay for a couple of minutes. I can\'t take care of it since it\'s not our cat.</p><p>On February 6, 2016, I went to check my gutter in my room around 2 AM. To my surprise, I saw 2 cute, white kittens stumbled right upon my very eyes! I didn\'t think I would believe the rumors but now I did! They look so adorable! Chichi was really pregnant and gave birth to those cute kittens. By February 10, 2016, the 2 kittens are on our house roof, meaning they saw the outside world for the 1st time. I captured a video of Chichi carrying 1 of them and they\'re very cute. By February 24, 2016, I grabbed them from the roof so that they can freely roam in the neighborhood around 10 AM. I placed them back on the roof before the day ended.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a id="chichi-the-stray-cat-ref-1"></a><sup>1</sup> - Chichi is the name of the cute, young girl in GMA\'s 2015 drama series, Little Nanay.</li>
            </ul>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('March 5, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-02-25',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Watching Taken Twice While Taking on a New Recipe',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s the last Sunday of the year. We\'ll be greeting 2016 in a couple of days. So I want to do something that will entertain me. That is, to watch movies! A movie marathon Sunday! I don\'t want to download movies and I\'d rather watch it online. Luckily, there are sites for that. Half of the afternoon was spent watching movies only. I watched The Maze Runner (which I already watched in SM), Taken and Taken 2 in that sequence.</p><p>After watching, I want to learn a new recipe. I cooked Beef with Broccoli on my own, with assistance from Mama (she boiled and chopped the beef). It\'s an easy recipe. The real challenge here is creating the sauce, not making it too sweet or too bitter. After cooking, Mama and Ate Anabel tried it. They said it was good! Not bad. We had our dinner at Tatay\'s house and apart from him, Patrick, Noel and Lola tasted it too! Noel found it delicious. It was a success!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2015-12-27',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Kuya Pedro\'s Birthday While Spending Quality Time For Facial',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s Kuya Pedro\'s birthday today. He spent it with his Mulawin friends. On the other hand, Tatay, Lola, Noel, Megan and Chloe went to the beach. Well, it\'s too early for summer. As for us, I went for a facial at Dermcare in SM with Mama and Patrick. As usual, the facial treatment is very expensive. Good thing Mama paid for our facial treatments. It lasted for 1 hour and the feeling is very exhilarating. It\'s been awhile since I had a facial with Mama. Haha!</p><p>We ate at Tokyo Tokyo for lunch. We were disappointed with their service because the serving time is very long. After having our lunch, Mama bought 300 Garena Shells each for me and Patrick. Then we went to DataBlitz to buy 1-year PSPlus membership each for me and Patrick worth P2,350 each. Thanks, Mama!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-01-03',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Mama\'s Initial Departure Back to Australia',
            'description' => '<p>Today marked Mama\'s departure to Australia. She, along with Mama Cathy, Tita Vina, Tita Carol, Lola, Chloe and Kuya Allan as their driver, rode Tatay\'s Toyota Fortuner vehicle. They left for Manila earlier because they couldn\'t wait us any longer. Me, Patrick and Daddy rode our Mitsubishi Evolution Lancer VIII car and left at 12:09 AM. I\'ve been sleeping for most of the trip.</p><p>We finally arrived at Manila. The last time I was here was when we also fetched Mama. At NAIA Terminal 2, Mama left at 8:25 AM. She plans to return by August again (although she is not sure yet). After Mama left, Mama Cathy opted not to come with us going back to Baguio. As for us, we headed straight to Valenzuela so that we can check how Lola Annie is holding up. We had a short-lived stay and left the house by 1:30 PM. Patrick drove the car until there. We arrived at the destination earlier than Kuya Allan. They arrived at 2:22 PM. We bid farewell to Daddy as he goes back home. We then went back to Baguio.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-01-11',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Cooking It Solo',
            'description' => '<p>I received an inquiry on my College Algebra book ad in olx.ph a couple of days ago. Yesterday, I received the payment from the buyer in LBC. Ate Kamille accompanied me. The book is sold for P250. Today, I ship that book. Getting the buyer\'s payment has been constantly delayed because I couldn\'t find the right time to claim it. At least it\'s settled yesterday. I shipped the book in JRS. The buyer was a woman and she\'s from Tacloban City.</p><p>I cooked my Beef with Broccoli recipe for the 2nd time. This time, the preparation and cooking was all done by myself. No help from anyone! I\'m starting to become more independent. Haha! There\'s more sauce and broccoli this time compared to when I first cooked it. One day, I\'ll be such a good cook that will soon become my passion.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-01-24',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Session in Bloom Woes',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s a massive traffic Sunday. Looks like a lot of tourists have been coming to Baguio lately. Panagbenga festival has started. The street dance and float parades will be held on the last weekend of the month. Well, there are a couple of weeks for the pre-Panagbenga activities. I\'m only looking forward for the yearly Session In Bloom, where Session Road is closed for 1 week. Lots of stalls will have their spot. It\'s mostly food! Delicious!</p><p>Anyway, I went to town to claim the money Daddy sent for our daily needs. I went to the Cebuana branch in Abanao Square to claim it. Unfortunately, I couldn\'t claim it because Tita Jhan placed my 3rd name on the form when she sent the money on February 2, 2016. So I went to the Cebuana branch in Pines Arcade and yes, no luck either. I told Daddy about this and he went to a Cebuana branch to change my name in the form by removing the 3rd name. My student ID only shows my 2 names, not my 3rd name. Afterwards, I claimed P1,500 from Daddy and this will be used for our grocery.</p><p>After claiming the money, I went home. To my surprise, the traffic was slightly reduced! Thank God, I wouldn\'t have to wait for so long just to get home.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-02-07',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Valentines\' Day 2016',
            'description' => '<p>For the 1st time, I had a Valentines date today. In the past few years, my Valentines Day was giving roses and chocolates o Mama and Mama Cathy. But this year, it\'s an actual date! I was having second thoughts on it, but I convinced myself that I should strike whilst the iron is hot. Because I may not get a chance if I delay it. My Valentines date is: Kamile! I didn\'t just considered her looks, but I invited her because I hardly invite her to my endeavors. We could have been a couple, if only I confessed my affection to her last October 17, 2015. It was a date in 2600 Gastropub, which I didn\'t come (because the agreement was that we talk face-to-face yet she invited a friend, so I refused to go). Anyway, I lost my chance.</p><p>It\'s ironic that most couples don\'t have roses. For Kamile, she deserves a rose. I bought white roses worth P250 in Harrison Road. I walked up all the way to SM, where she is impatiently waiting. We watched the Deadpool movie in Cinema 1. It was very hilarious and the audience really enjoyed it. The cinema was full, we had to sit by the steps for there are no more vacant seats available. I treated our movie tickets while she treated our McDo fries and drinks. Then we ate at Don Henrico\'s for I got hungry. My treat once again. She ordered Combo 1 and I ordered Combo 3.</p><p>I accompanied her in getting a taxi. She said she can go home by herself yet I insisted to accompany her. Women should always be kept safe. I worried for safety of Kamile especially with the increasing rape cases at night. Afterwards, I went home extremely happy.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-02-14',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Kuya Jov\'s Birthday Bash in Lemonet',
            'description' => '<p>Today, I have sold my Uniqlo shirt, Phat Farm shirt and Lee sweatshirt for P700 through a meetup in front of Step Learning Academy. Ironically, I could reach Tita Gemma\'s house in just a couple of steps. The buyer is a construction worker who is working on a building in front of Step Learning Academy. The Uniqlo shirt was a gift by Mama Cathy when she was in for a trip to Singapore. The Phat Farm shirt was finally sold after more than a year since being posted online (it\'s one of the 1st items that I intended to sold). The Lee sweatshirt is stuffed in my wardrobe that I never wore at all, so why not just sell it for extra income.</p><p>By 6:40 PM, I went to Lemonet to celebrate Kuya Jov\'s birthday. Foods! Fried chicken and pansit is tonight\'s menu. Apart from Kuya Jov, we have Ken, Jics, Tudy, Zed and Reyn in attendance. Ricky and Kuya Alfie didn\'t come though. They missed out on the foods really badly.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-02-26',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Sweaty and Smelly',
            'description' => '<p>Me and Billy took a ride from a Trancoville jeep in front of Baguio Cathedral going to Chopping Burgh. I ordered Say Cheese with fries worth P162 and Coke Light for P30. After having lunch, I accompanied Billy in Altitude gym at Mount Crest Hotel. We walked all the way going there. Then walked again to Burnham Park and finally back to UC. It was an exhausting yet fun walk. I was seating because of that.</p><p>I attended my Firewalls and Network Security &amp; ECON 1 classes full of sweat. I didn\'t realized I smell this bad. I was even wearing the 3/4 sweatshirt that Ate Kamille gave me. Finally, I went home. I couldn\'t stand my own stench so I changed my clothes immediately. I played Digimon Story: Cyber Sleuth in the PS4 for the rest of the night.</p><p>Ate Kamille came into the house and needed help in fixing her slow browsing issue on her laptop. Things I did included disabling unnecessary startup services, uninstalled unused programs and installed Google Chrome. None of these worked until I looked it up on the internet. It suggested to untick the option "Use hardware accelerator" in Google Chrome settings. It finally worked!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-03-22',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'My 2016 Birthday Celebration',
            'description' => '<p>I celebrate my 21st birthday today. Wow, I become more mature every year. Haha! However, the 1st few hours started badly. I had to sleep at 5:28 AM because a technician took too long to configure the router for resolving no connectivity. Yet all those hours waiting for it to be resolved ended up unsuccessful. Tita Carol sent in that technician who didn\'t feel ashamed that I needed to rest for he was using my computer.</p><p>Daddy arrived around lunch time. Tatay was surprised for his sudden appearance. Daddy was the one who fixed our connectivity, much to the chagrin of a technician. Ate Anabel went out to buy cake and palabok, for this is Tita Carol\'s birthday gifts to me. I went to town by 3:14 PM to meet with Ryzher. We strolled around SM and talked about topics such as BAA, video games, pranking etc. Then I went to Zola as Kamile is waiting for me there. I told Ryzher not to come but it looks like Kamile wanted to invite other people. Bad mistake.</p><p>I successfully invited Ken and Zel while Kamile invited her friends Nicole and Stephen. The 3 San Mig Light promo was treated by Kamile, shared P200. Kamile and I wanted to try the Breezer beer, ordered 3 beers for P210. Nicole shared P300 for the next 12 San Mig Light promo. In order of departure: Kamile, Ken and Zel, Kamile being the last and Zel as the first. Me and Kamile\'s 2 friends parted ways together. Went home before 2 AM. The cake and palabok are on the table. I\'ll eat them once I get up. Time to rest!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('May 11, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-04-09',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 3,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Poem #12',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Kahinaan"</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">I.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sa isang silid, napansin ko itong dalaga</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Mukhang mabigat ang damdaming kinakarga</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nahihiyang lumapit sa kanya</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hindi masabi ang aking linya</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">II.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nabihag niya ang puso kong inosente</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Pakiramdam ko ay parang nakuryente</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Nakatitig sa kanya habang napaisip</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">"Hininga ko ay biglang sumikip"</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">III.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Haplos ng buhok niyang napakabango</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Diretso sa puso niya ako\'y tutungo</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sa ganda niya ako\'y napatingin</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Ang pagbago ng ihip ng hangin</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hindi masabi ang totoong nararamdaman</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sa iyong pagsulyap, ako\'y kinakabahan</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Kapag nakikita ka, ako\'y napapatula</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Hindi pala ito panaginip, aking naalala</p>
            <p>This poem is the first poem I wrote in Filipino language.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 4, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-04-28',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 3,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Poem #13',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Deep Blue Ocean"</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">I.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I looked far to the deep blue ocean</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">My thoughts running wildly</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Stood ashore to see waves in motion</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">With fists gripped in tightly</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">II.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I told myself how things easily fade</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">These had been my serenity</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The memories that was once my jade</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Now are nothing but serendipity</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">III.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Calm like an ocean, I see</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Its splashes rejuvenate my tomorrow</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Rage like the waves, they flee</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Sought for happiness, yet found sorrow</p>
            <p style="text-align:left;">IV.</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">I left the ocean with an eased mind</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Yet repeatedly turning my back</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">The memories I can\'t leave behind</p>
                <p style="margin-left:2em;">Those that I can still track</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 4, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-07-05',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #10',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Through the fire and flames"</p><p>October 19, 2010, will be remembered as a disastrous day. My room was burned as the flames consumed my room to the brim. I lost my computer, 2nd year books, PS3-only keyboard, bed and most especially the HDTV and DVD. Ironically, the date itself is special. It was <a href="#through-the-fire-and-flames-ref-1"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Melisa\'s</span><sup>1</a></sup> birthday, the person I\'m sinning against. I was the one who threw her books and stole her dictionary. So I believed God punished me by burning my room. I dearly paid the price.</p><p>That day, there was no electricity. We had to use candles for a couple of nights. It was already raining since last week due to the <a href="#through-the-fire-and-flames-ref-2"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">Ondoy-Pepeng</span><sup>2</a></sup> onslaught. At around 6 PM, Patrick left the candle on my computer and followed me downstairs, going to Tatay\'s house and stayed there until dinner. By 6:37 PM (time on my watch), I heard Tita Carol screaming that there\'s fire in my room. Tatay rushed to my room and kicked the door hard (he thought I was there). Kuya Tarsy extinguished the flames. Everything but my C.R. and the PS3 (luckily it was covered with a cloth) was burned. That PS3 was the most expensive possession I had back then! Up to this day, it was such an unforgettable experience.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><a id="through-the-fire-and-flames-ref-1"></a><sup>1</sup> - she\'s my Korean classmate from 2nd Year and 3rd Year who\'s having a crush on me. Lol.</li>
                <li><a id="through-the-fire-and-flames-ref-2"></a><sup>2</sup> - this was the strongest typhoon ever back then. Typhoon Ondoy came in first before Typhoon Pepeng did.</li>
            </ul>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 9, 2016 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-08-09',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #11',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Derma Bonding"</p><p>One of the rarest moments I do is bonding with my brother. This is one of the most unique bonding moments I have experienced. Back on August 3, 2016, Patrick invited me to have facial at SM. He showed me 2 stubs of free facial cares at Dermcare in SM. Looks amazing! He originally would have facial with the friend who gave him the free stubs but he backed out, according to Patrick. So I took the stub for a free facial care. We presented the stubs at Dermcare and the type of facial care we had was diamond peeling. It wasn\'t our first time here though (we were with Mama on January 3, 2016).</p><p>We felt so great after that exhilarating facial care (I had a reddish face after they removed a lot of blackheads). It\'s greater to bond with my brother. I felt so fresh after that facial thanks to the stubs given by Patrick.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-06-11',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Hotel 45 vs. 45 Hotel: A Night of Bad Service',
            'description' => '<p>I went to town and walked until reaching SLU Gate 1. I waited for Ryzher at the 7-11 branch in front of it. While waiting, I saw my batchmate Gian crossing the pedestrian lane out of the blue. I haven\'t seen him since our Grade 6 graduation ball in 2008. When Ryzher arrived, we went inside the Mineski internet cafe for the 1st time but we didn\'t play. Gian said the membership costs P100. Members pay P17/hour while non-members pay P25/hour. We left Gian at Mineski while me and Ryzher went to TNC. Ryzher had to register a new account with a default password of "ddd". I still have my old account there. Played for around 4 hours. I was able to play Skyrim and Dead Island Riptide for the 1st time on their PC version.</p><p>After playing, we walked all the way to Session Road. At a 7-11 branch, I bought a Marlboro Black case worth P70 for Kamile and mineral water worth P10 for me. We went to the Jollibee branch in Harrison Road to use their comfort rooms without ordering anything. Haha. Kamile asked me to meet her at "Hotel 45" so me and Ryzher went to Upper Session Road. To our dismay, she\'s not there. She told us to go to "45 Hotel" (which at first thought that they\'re the same, but they aren\'t). That place is somewhere in Lower Session Road so we walked all the way down there. It\'s located near a Levi\'s store and finally, she\'s there. There is a big difference between "Hotel 45" and "45 Hotel". Lesson learned.</p><p>There\'s a bar inside that is old-looking and cramped yet the good things is that there are dartboards and you could sing in the karaoke too. There\'s also billiard tables at the floor below us. I ordered a 500ml Red Horse beer for P70 and a San Mig Light beer for Ryzher (my treat) for P60. Ryzher\'s beer didn\'t arrive yet though. Kamile said she wants to "transfer" but "bid goodbye" to her classmates in Engineering. She and her friend Marissa went to Zola instead.</p><p>Now me and Ryzher are left with the people we don\'t even know. Ryzher got the number of a hot chick behind our table. My review? I don\'t care how old it looks like, it was the poor service I hated. I called and told the waitress twice to send Ryzher\'s beer and we thought she heard it. Because of impatience, I just went to the counter and told that same waitress that same order. Lo and behold, I got the beer. A crap service for such an old-looking bar.</p><p>After 45 Hotel, we went to Zola by 8 PM. Kamile, Marissa and her other friend Ched is already there. I spoke with Ryzher for like 90% of my time there. "Damn, this was a girls\' night out.", I told myself. So by 9 PM, me and Ryzher parted ways. I went home and he went to SM to meet with his family.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-04-20',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'House Visit by Classmates and Friends',
            'description' => '<p>Today is the 3rd day of the 3rd Trimester SY 2015-2016. 2 days removed from the 1st day of classes. Around lunch time, I went to the market to buy 5 pieces of oranges worth P67 and 3 dozens of longganisa worth P468. It\'s my first time to buy oranges on my own. I went to school only to find out that Ma\'am Quitaleg isn\'t around for my only Saturday class Web Development 2 (lab). Instead, I went to SM to stroll alone. I inquired about the PS4 game, The Division in DataBlitz and the clerk said it costs P2,195. Then I went to Octagon to check out some headsets. They have Razer products out there.</p><p>Kamile texted and urged me to meet her at Pizza Hut in SM. We ate at Chowking. I ordered Beef Chao Fan worth P85 and she ordered Pork Chao Fan with dumplings worth P92. She insisted that Ange, Nicole and herself visit our house tonight. I initially declined due to a messy room but agreed in the end. Then we went back to the UC gym to "wait" for Ange. She didn\'t show up though. Kamile decided we just go to my jeep terminal and wait for them in the house. Yet she changed her mind and waited for Nicole. She came and we proceeded to fetch Ange from Loakan (I thought she was at school). After fetching her, we had a taxi ride to my house. Nicole\'s treat for the fare.</p><p>Ange and Nicole went to Armar\'s Place to buy gin while me and Kamile bought 3 Nestea grape flavor juice for our chaser. At home, I felt ashamed for such a messy room. I told them to smoke outside because my ventilation isn\'t good. Kamile left around 10 PM. Me, Ange and Nicole went to the Night Market to eat. Sisig, mami and isaw is what we ate. We parted ways. Ange left first followed by Nicole and lastly, me.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-05-13',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'The Colds That Wouldn\'t Quit',
            'description' => '<p>I attended my STS class with severe colds. It has been like this since yesterday. I went home to do the financial analysis of our project in Project Management class. Sadly, I wasn\'t able to attend the class because I ended up with nothing. So I just watched some WWE videos in YouTube instead. After that, I did a group activity presentation for my Web Development 2 class. My groupmates were Adrian and Reyn. I asked Reyn to do it but she texted me and said she has a class, I volunteered to do it instead.</p><p>I attended my Web Development 2 class and surprisingly, my colds were "healed". No, not really. The colds were just dormant. Our group is the first to present our answers to the questions in our class\' e-book using a powerpoint. My classmates\' presentation of their powerpoints had images while our group has none of it. I really considered adding images but because of time constraints, our presentation was pure text.</p><p>I went home and realized that my colds are back. Well, you could say worse than awhile ago. Each time I blow my nose, I just kept on sneezing. It hurts my nose.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-06-26',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Cooking, Coding, and Ate Cora',
            'description' => '<p>Today is Android Studio day. I\'m developing a mobile application that tests the user\'s logic and speed as they answer a series of questions. It\'s a simple application that is designed to all types of users. From children to elders. The application is our project for Project Management class. I\'m on my seventh day. In the afternoon, I cooked Pork Sarciado for the first time. I let Ate Kamille taste it. She approves the taste! Not bad for an apprentice!</p><p>Mama Cathy went up to the house and noticed the Pork Sarciado on the table. She exclaimed how thoughtful and kind I was to cook for our dinner. Haha. After dinner, I got an unexpected call. A call from Ate Cora, whom I\'ve never seen since I was Grade 6. Come to think of it, it\'s a very long time! She asked about Mama and wanted to send regards to her.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-07-16',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'A Successful Voter Registration',
            'description' => '<p>I sold my Phat Farm pants for P250 by meetup in Sakura Bar at the back of Skyworld bazaar. The scheduled time to meet was 9 AM however I woke up late so it was pushed back to 11 AM instead. Since July 18, I\'ve sold 3 items by meetups. The Marks and Spencer polo was sold for P150 by meetup in Porta Vaga and my FUBU jacket was sold for P350 by meetup in the BDO branch before going to SM. That\'s a whopping P750!</p><p>Heavy rainfall greeted my Thursday afternoon. Kuya Buckie accompanied me for the registration in the upcoming local elections on October 31, 2016. It was my first time to be a registered voter. He also treated our fare in the jeep. After my registration, I went to school. To my surprise, we have no lab classes due to evaluation of the instructors. I\'m heading straight home then.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-07-20',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Windows Upgrade, But for my Computer',
            'description' => '<p>The last Saturday of the 3rd Trimester SY 2015-2016 will use the MWF schedule. I have classes for STS and Project Management today. In STS, we watched a documentary on the evolution of agriculture back to the traditional practices to the modern era. Other than that, we had our attendance checked in Project Management, the last group presented their project. It\'s a mobile application that teaches its users on simple mathematics such as the basic operations and exponents. I have no class for Web Development 2.</p><p>By 3:45 PM, I went to Bohemian Cafe to drink with Airwin. He urged me to invite friends. I contacted everyone I know who drinks beer to come over. Those who are in my phonebook. Yet none of them wanted to drink. Airwin contacted his friends too but no luck either. Looks like they don\'t feel the Saturday vibes today. Anyway, we drank 5 bottles each and went home around 6 PM.</p><p>At home, I utilized the free Windows 10 upgrade on my computer. Today is the last day for it. The interface was well-built and I made the right choice.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-07-29',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'First Stint at Playing PS2 Games on PC',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s National Heroes\' Day! A holiday to celebrate the triumph of our brave warriors who fought for the welfare of the country. Kudos! Their bravery and valor will always be recognized. We salute them and big thanks for saving our country. Today marks the first time I played PS2 games on PC using an emulator. I downloaded the PCSX2 program on the internet. I watched a step-by-step tutorial on YouTube in using the PCSX2 program. The video was very detailed and it had all the files I needed for the emulator to work.</p><p>I have been planning to play PS2 games on emulator since the start of 2015 but was very doubtful due to its nature of viruses. Today, I finally had the courage to do that after 1 year. The first game I played is Final Fantasy XII. I downloaded the game from the internet. This file is around 2.7 GB. Because of my anticipation, I was awake until 7 AM the next morning just playing. The story reached until Vaan, Balthier and Fran reached the Nalbina Dungeon imprisonment.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('June 18, 2017 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-08-29',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Monday Woes',
            'description' => '<p>Waking up on a Monday morning is very stressful because I had to get up in bed so early to start the week. I paid P150 to Kamile for the ticket of Miss Baguio 2016 pageant held on September 17, 2016 at Baguio Convention Center. She didn\'t win though.</p><p>After 6 years, I\'ve played my Nintendo DS that was shelfed for too long. I played Metal Slug 7. I didn\'t even know that there was a Metal Slug on this platform. There are only 7 missions in the game.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-09-19',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Washing Away',
            'description' => '<p>Today marks the first time I washed my own clothes since November 8, 2015. Ate Anabel has once again escaped last October 23, 2016 that marked Chloe\'s 4th birthday. I used Lola\'s washing machine since Mama\'s washing machine is slightly damaged. I enlisted the help of Kuya Pedro on operating the washing machine. The appliance has more useful functionalities than what I used before. This washing machine is very efficient: wash, rinse and spin all at the same time. It only takes 40 minutes! The first 26 minutes does the 1st washing and the last 14 minutes will have the 2nd washing and spin. You can then hung it and let it dry.</p><p>After washing my clothes, I went to play League of Legends. I bought Lucian from the in-game store and he\'s the only champion I used for this day. Lucian overload!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-10-29',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Achievement Unlocked: Nab the Proper Taste of an Adobo Meal',
            'description' => '<p>I have made a great personal achievement today. It\'s a small thing but big in terms of my personal development. I finally got the taste of Adobo! Despite being the 1st dish I\'ve ever learned to cook 2 years ago, I failed to capture the real taste. It\'s either too sweet or too bitter. Today, I got this extra-ordinary confidence to try my luck on getting the right taste on this classic dish and I was successful. I endured the long process it took to finish. Kuya Buckie chopped an onion in half for me. I used Facebook live video to celebrate this small achievement.</p><p>Later on, I was supposed to buy 10 pandesal at Mulawin but it was closed. Well, that sucks. Instead, I bought a 12 oz. coke for myself.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-11-09',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Proctor Evaluation Week',
            'description' => '<p>Teacher evaluation week! I\'m one of the four proctors for today\'s evaluations alongside Harold and 2 others. Me and Harold were in-charge at room M307. I arrived before 9 AM and by 9:21 AM, I had to go home by riding a taxi (to take a dump since I couldn\'t bear the stomach ache anymore). I left my bag at the room though. I got back quickly.</p><p>Before lunch, Ma\'am Quitaleg asked me to buy our meals at KFC. She handed me P500 then off I went. I ordered 4 flavor shots worth P80, 6 chicken burger sandwiches worth P35 for a total of P570. I had to pay the P70 shortage. The official receipt is charged to "UC-CITCS". I left the receipt to Ma\'am Quitaleg\'s desk then distributed the flavor shot meals to all proctors. Harold exclaimed that it\'s not enough for him haha.</p><p>I saw old classmates from CEA coming to M307 such as Czha, Melvz and Jeohmar. By 4 PM, Ma\'am Quitaleg urged us to eat the burgers already. Yummy! After eating, we went to Ma\'am Dela Cruz for the advising of our Capstone 1 document. Just a few more revisions! By 5 PM, we got the "go signal" for dismissal. This day is so tiring yet exhilarating!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-11-17',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'First Stint at Pisonet Shops and Malabon Fair',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s my 3rd meetup with Alyza today. I wore the new gray Baleno sweatshirt I bought from MOA 2 days ago. I asked Daddy and Patrick to bring me to Malabon again and I arrived at Alyza\'s house by 5:13 PM. We decided to spend our afternoon together at the fair near Robinson\'s Town Malabon mall, which is only around 5 minutes from Alyza\'s house. All rides in the fair costs P40 per head. I treated her for all the rides such as the viking, octofish, ferris wheel and the wacky worm party. I personally liked the viking ride.</p><p>After having fun at the fair, we went back to her house. She introduced me to her stepfather and uncle. They invited me to drink a 500ml Red Horse beer with them to which I agreed. We had long conversations and I think they\'re very friendly to guests. After finishing 1 glass of beer, we proceeded to an unlikely computer shop just in front of their house. Referred to as "pisonet" shops, you drop P1 coins into a slot to keep your time running. Each coin gives 6 minutes and when it runs out, the screen turns black unless you put another P1 coin in it. 1 hour in this shop is equivalent to 10 P1 coins. Comparing this with regular computer shops, it\'s a lot cheaper!</p><p>I left Alyza\'s house by 12:29 AM. This is the longest time I\'ve spent my day with Alyza compared to the previous 2 meetings.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2016-12-30',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Coding and Kittens!',
            'description' => '<p>I was awakened by a distant noise coming from the main gate. I stood up and checked it out. I saw Megan, Chloe, Kuya Pedro and the other kids outside. To my surprise, there were 2 tiny black kittens on a cardboard box! Kuya Pedro rescued the cute kittens from the roof this morning. Megan, Chloe and the other kids were the first to discover the lost cats. It was believed to be Chichi\'s offsprings because of the kittens\' noses that\'s similar to Chichi. I let the kittens drink milk and pet them gently so that I could get their trust faster and easier.</p><p>Today is also coding day. The Personal Website that I have been working on has transformed to have PHP support and additional functionalities. I used XAMPP as my web server, Notepad++ as my text editor and MySQL as my database management tool. Lo and behold, my Walkthroughs page transformed nicely! I\'ll be adding more pages soon.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-01-15',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Sad Day for Kittens and not Getting Another Shirt',
            'description' => '<p>In just a span of 6 days, 2 additional kittens have been welcomed to our home! The cat population has doubled. Both kittens have gray and white colors. One of the kittens is significantly bigger than the other 3 kittens yet it\'s the most frightened cat. Anyway, I let them drink milk as my welcome gift for them. After a couple of hours, the biggest cat unwaringly left the house while I was dressing up. It happened when Megan, Chloe and the other kids left our main gate opened. It came in so unexpectedly and I was saddened for the day.</p><p>I went to school by 1:30 PM to get the Google shirt that Tristen promised to hand it to me. I thought it was the purple Google I/O shirts that I never claimed last year but it turned out to be the black Google DevFest shirts instead. Tristen gave me a chance to obtain the shirt but I opted not to get another piece since I already received the same shirt last year. Meanwhile, Zel arrived and opted to get another Google DevFest shirt (she already owned one though).</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-01-21',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'E-Commerce Culmination First Half',
            'description' => '<p>This is it! Today is the presentation of each teams\' business reports. It\'s the last day of the E-commerce class of Team B. I never realized it would be the last official day of class meeting. But wait! Hold your horses! Our Korean instructor, Mr. Sung, said that we\'ll exchange with Team A and attend the Design Thinking Principle class at U301 (our E-commerce class was held at U201, which is a lab room). Oh, I will surely miss this room.</p><p>After the announcement, Mr. Sung lend the class to the UC Theater for a short briefing on the assignment of booths for tomorrow\'s Korean event entitled "TAL-K Festival" to be held here. Then when the briefing is done, we went back to U201 for Mr. Sung treated us snacks and softdrinks for the whole class. My Filipino friends were expecting pizza per team but they got junk foods instead.</p><p>I went home a little sad. What\'s even worst? This black cat bugged me off when he scratched my leg for no reason. He was trying to climb on my lap forcefully. Out of frustration, I hurt the cat. He ends up cowering in fear.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-01-26',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Gaming Day and Monthsary Celebration',
            'description' => '<p>Happy 1st monthsary to me and my 3rd girlfriend, Alyza Dosal! I was able to sneak the first monthsary greeting for the day. She was in awe! We played against each other in an ARAM mode in LOL. That\'s our kind of date actually. We may be miles apart, but close to each others\' hearts! How I\'d wish we see each other on this special day. Soon!</p><p>I asked permission from my brother if I could play his PS4. He\'s not at home though, but rather at Manila. He\'s having vacation there and I don\'t know when he will be back though. As always, I played Digimon Story: Cyber Sleuth. I also gave the 8th weekly salary of Kuya Pedro. Apart from all these, I simply enjoyed the day with our Design Thinking Principle class awhile ago.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-02-01',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'My First Day Attending a NIIT module',
            'description' => '<p>I\'m excited for my first day in my Web Design module class in NIIT. The school is very far. I had to ride 2 jeeps to get there. So I decided to leave home 1 hour before the class starts so that I won\'t be late. To enroll, I paid P6,650 (5% discount of P7,000) on January 31. My instructor is Sir Don.</p><p>Sir Don briefed me on what my module is about. The module tackles HTML, CSS, JavaScript, JQuery, Bootstrap, MySQL and PHP (wow, that\'s a lot!). He assessed me on how knowledgable I am in web development. Because I have a decent knowledge in HTML, CSS and Bootstrap, the module will be fast-paced. Actual coding starts next meeting. For now, I\'m dismissed early.</p><p>To get to the town plaza, I took a Trancoville jeep. Manila tourists rode the jeep and are very noisy. I conversed with a female teenager and asked where the jeep will stop. She said that there are jeeps that passes through SM and jeeps that unloads passengers in Harrison Road. The pretty teenager dropped off at Gov. Pack and I dropped off from NBI.</p><p>In SM, I watched Resident Evil: The Final Chapter alone. My favorite movie series will have its last movie (for now). I\'m satisfied with the battle sequences and those nasty-looking BOWs made it so badass! I went home happily.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-02-04',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Last Day for Submission of Graduation Applications',
            'description' => '<p>Today is the 2nd day of on-site selling in our Design Thinking Principle class. We had our post-Valentines Day booth at the UC Canteen. We\'re selling tumblers, teddy bears, DIY letters and we have a photo booth as well. I got an application for graduation form from the CITCS office. Seeing the form, I need a passport-sized picture and an NSO-certified birth certificate. Imagine this, today is the last day for submission of graduation applications. I had to rush them before 5:30 PM today.</p><p>I had my picture taken at Babes Studio in Porta Vaga. Then I went home to get the NSO-certified copy of my birth certificate. With less than 1 hour left, I need to find the last document in Mama\'s room. It was a hard and tedious search that consumed all my time. I hurriedly got a jeep. When I got to Session Road, I retrieved the pictures, photocopied my birth certificate and tried to submit my form. However, it\'s too late. The secretary already left. Bad luck.</p><p>I ate shawarma on my way home. Surprisingly, Ate Kamille rode the same jeep as I do. At home, we had no internet nor dial tone. What a way to end the day.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-02-15',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Mini-Celebration With Fellow Graduates',
            'description' => '<p>I am one of the proctors for this trimester\'s teacher evaluation. I am in-charge of room M305 alone (I was in-charge of the same room with Harold yesterday). Around lunch time, I saw Ida evaluating on my room while I was having my lunch! Our lunch came from the canteen, Adobo and Chicken Curry meals care of Ma\'am Quitaleg. It is delicious though.</p><p>After our proctor duties, I treated my fellow interns a buy-one, take-one pizza from Pizza Hut worth P419. I played hide-and-seek with Darian and Kazia, even to the point of telling them that I went home. Hahaha! It was during this time that I formally conversed with Kazia (after so long of not talking to her). They weren\'t able to come.</p><p>There were 6 of us. Zel, Jonah and Onie. George and RJ left earlier and wasn\'t able to have pizza with us. The pizza we ordered were bacon and cheeseburger flavors. Jonah treated us a 1.75L Coke and we ate the pizzas at SM Foodcourt. We parted ways separately. Jonah and Onie were left behind at SM while Zel and me parted ways at Session Road. Everyone thanked me for the treat!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-03-21',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Manila Escapade',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s Easter Sunday on a rainy afternoon. It\'s my 2nd day in Manila (I commuted alone yesterday at 3:32 AM and arrived at 8:44 AM at Barangay Camachile in Quezon City). Alyza expected me today so we had our 1st meetup (4th overall) as official couples. I was accompanied by Kuya JE. We dropped off at Monumento to buy 1 white rose each for Alyza\'s mother and grandmother then 3 red roses for Alyza herself. Then we rode an Acacia Malabon jeep, dropped off at Robinsons Town Mall Malabon and rode a pedicab to her place. Their place is badly flooded.</p><p>Once there, I gave the white roses to her mother and grandmother. The latter was very delighted while the former is drinking along with Alyza\'s stepfather. Kuya JE left and I was invited to drink their local hard liquor called Pares and 3 cases of Red Horse beer. I stole passionate kisses to my girlfriend multiple times. After drinking, I accompanied her to buy Sisig and barbeques somewhere far. We ate the meals to Lola Babies\' (her grandmother) house. Then we watched Wansapanataym before leaving. Alyza accompanied me until Monumento so that I get used to commuting in Manila.</p><p>At Monumento, I texted Kuya JE to fetch me, however, he did\'t reply. In the meantime, we stopped at 7-11 and bought a mineral water. I\'ve already finished my mineral water and Kuya JE hasn\'t replied to my texts yet. We stayed inside 7-11 and chatted until Alyza said she needs to go home already.</p><p>I accompanied Alyza to their jeep terminal and bid goodbye along with a kiss. I decided to commute alone. I went to the jeep terminal on the opposite side of 7-11 by crossing the overpass. Luckily, it passes through Karuhatan. This is my first time to commute alone in Manila at night. I arrived home safe and sound.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('July 22, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-04-16',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 7,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Unholy Confessions #12',
            'description' => '<p style="text-align:center;">"Formal Attire Gone Wrong"</p><p>Last April 14, 2016, I experienced one of the worst humiliations in my entire life. I was wearing my formal attire for my Technopreneurship class at 10:00 - 11:15 AM. After our online business reporting, I headed to Lemonet shop to play LOL. I played 1 normal game in solo queue and 1 ranked game with Ricky. During the ranked game, I felt extremely tense because I want to defecate. I played as Tristana and Ricky played as Jax. We were able to finish the match and win it too. Just as I was about to walk up the stairs, I lost my control and took a crap on where I was standing!</p><p>I couldn\'t resist it! Things happened really fast. I rushed immediately to the CR. Boy, what a huge mess! I was wearing my formal attire and cleaning my dump in the toilet. Eventually, a janitress brought tissues and Domex so that I can clean my own mess. She also bought me shorts to help me change. After that horrible mess, I called Ken through the phone and told him to hail me a taxi so I can go home. Luckily, my polo doesn\'t have crap on it. It was awkward walking with leather shoes while wearing shorts and it doesn\'t get nastier when taking a dump and have that dump seen by many people. Humiliating! Up to now, I was never able to pay that janitress back and I still use the shorts to this very day.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-08-02',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'First Stint at Commuting Solo',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s my first time to commute alone in Manila in the morning. No need to rely on Daddy to bring me to Alyza\'s place. I rode a Sta. Maria jeep going to Monumento then Acacia Malabon jeep going to Alyza\'s place. She let me stay in Lola Babies\' house and told me to wait for her to take a bath. After that, we took a pedicab going to Herbalife where her other grandmother, Lola Mode, is working. The place is extremely far. I was amazed when we got there.</p><p>Herbalife is a nutrition company that is focused on healthy living and weight loss by offering their clients healthy fruit shakes to lose weight. They have a weekly program that keeps track of their clients\' progress. I was introduced to Lola Mode. Although not as friendly as Lola Babies, she offered me to try their fruit shakes for free. I accepted. Alyza went to the counter and served me a Vanilla shake. I learned that her family has another house in Longos (where Alyza\'s father lives with another family). No doubt her parents are far from each other. After staying in Herbalife, we went back to Catmon. She asked permission from her mother if she could sleepover at our place. She was granted permission.</p><p>Me and Alyza went to Monumento. We stopped at 7-11 to buy a Del Monte Four Seasons juice drink. We chatted for a bit then commuted back home to Karuhatan. She was feeling nervous because I introduced her to Daddy, Patrick and Tita Jhan. She was well-perceived by them. This night marks her 1st sleepover at our house and there\'s more to come.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-04-18',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Fighting Urges: Walking Steady and Slowly Out of School',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s the 2nd week of classes for the 3rd Tri SY 2016-2017. I had my lunch at Manny Bee\'s eatery. I don\'t know what the dish is called but it tastes awful. After my lunch, I went back to school and bought Mountain Dew worth P18. In the remaining hours, I waited for my Network Fundamentals class (a subject replacement for Mobile Technology) at 5:30 - 6:45 PM. I saw Ken along the hallway and sat beside me. He is with his newfound friends. While chatting, I am feeling stomach aches. We transferred to the gym to watch a volleyball match between 2 universities that is unfamiliar to us.</p><p>During the 1st match, my stomach aches start to get worst. I had 30 minutes left before my class starts. Minute after minute, the pain is excruciating. I was able to hold it for a few minutes before giving up and decided to defecate at a public restroom. I told Ken that I needed to leave because I couldn\'t bear the stomach ache anymore. I left UC steadily and carefully.</p><p>It was a rainy afternoon. I went to a public restroom that I know of (in Melvin Jones Grandstand). Bad news. I found it closed. Because of the excruciating pain, I forced myself to tread the muddy soccer field for the sake of desperation. My gray Converse sneakers was so muddy and it didn\'t have the fresh, factory look anymore. I was able to find another public restroom (which is nearer to UC) near the police station. I walked fast yet careful so that I don\'t poop at the wrong place. I made it on time. It\'s my 1st time to defecate at a public restroom. I had 2 dippers full of water to ensure that no poop gets left behind then I went inside one of the cubicles. Inside, I released my "inner demons". It was such a success! I felt great again! Energized. Then I started cleaning my dirt with the 1st dipper, wiped it with tissue, poured the last half of the water, wiped again and repeated the same steps with the 2nd dipper.</p><p>For P12, it was all worth it. However, I finished at around 5:30 PM and I still went back to UC to make it in class. Unfortunately, I didn\'t attend anymore as I was late. Instead, I went to a CR and washed off the mud from my shoes then went home. It was a successful day!</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-05-16',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'An Incorrect Item Bought',
            'description' => '<p>It\'s my first time to buy an item online (via shipping). I paid P671 at Palawan Express on June 15 (P650 selling price and P21 sending tax). It\'s a payment for a G-Star light gray bomber jacket I saw at olx.ph. Me and the seller\'s main communication is through Viber since she uses a Smart number and my unlitext promo is for Globe numbers only.</p><p>I\'m excited to see the bomber jacket I bought online. I claimed the package at JRS today. I went home immediately to check it out. The bomber jacket was packed nicely but when I saw how it looked, I realized it was wrong. I was sent a dark gray bomber jacket instead of the lighter version. I complained this to a seller and had a misunderstanding. Looks like my original order went out of stock so she sent the darker version instead. In our communication, she offered to have the bomber jacket replaced within 7 days only out of good will. I looked at her ads in olx.ph again for a replacement however, nothing interested me.</p><p>Besides having the wrong item sent, the sleeves are tight. Kudos for a nice packaging though I\'ll just wear this for some time then sell it.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('August 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-06-19',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Lola Rowena\'s Visit and a Positive Feedback From a Buyer',
            'description' => '<p>I received a rude awakening from Ate Kamille today. She is yelling outside the house to open our door so that she could come and inform me of something very important. Lola Rowena is coming over to Baguio to visit Tatay. She will be here for 2 days. Apparently, there\'s no vacant room at Tatay\'s house and Mama\'s room is free at the moment. Ate Kamille told me that Tatay opted to let Lola Rowena sleep in Mama\'s room. I cleaned Mama\'s room including her CR. Lola Rowena arrived just in the nick of time. I finished cleaning upstairs but I had to go to town. It seems that Tita Vina fetched them using Tatay\'s vehicle. Looks like Lola Rowena won\'t be sleeping upstairs alone, she\'s accompanied by an unnamed woman. Anyway, I headed to town.</p><p>I sold my Delkin HS-300 leather headset for P200. The meetup is at Prime Hotel and I arrived at 1:53 PM (I was late for nearly an hour since the meetup time was supposed to be at 1 PM). The buyer exclaimed his gratitude through a text when he got home. The sounds were amazing! Before going home, I had a Chicken Burrito for takeout at Turks. I ate it at the Cathedral then went home.</p><p>When I went home, Lola Rowena and company left for Vigan. Tita Vina accompanied them again. Although I didn\'t see them today, they won\'t be sleeping in Mama\'s room. Lucky.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-06-24',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'The R\'s: Razer and Ryzher',
            'description' => '<p>I attended my Mobile Technology class at 8:55 AM. I am nearly done with my audio project. I just need to finish the last chapter of my script. The submission will be on Wednesday, 2 days from now. After my class, I headed to Shiverdrift shop to play with Ryzher. I opted to walk all the way going there (I didn\'t ride the Trancoville jeep that passes there). When I arrived, I removed my jacket, cap, watch and wristband due to a tiring walk. I installed Infestation: The New Z (a free-to-play game on Steam) in my computer terminal and Ryzher played Dota 2 while waiting for me. We played for around 3 hours before leaving.</p><p>I dropped off at the Harrison Overpass and Ryzher went to UC. When I got to our jeep terminal, I realized that I forgot my Razer Nabu X wristband at Shiverdrift. For some reason, I didn\'t feel surprised or nervous at all. I never bothered coming back for it and went straight home. Once I got home, I told Ryzher about it. Frankly, he was concerned and urged me to get it back because it may still be there. His concern pushed me to go back and claim it. I guess there is still hope!</p><p>I took a taxi ride going straight to Shiverdrift. It was traffic but not once that I ever got concerned for a wristband. The thought never crossed my mind. I arrived at the shop. Lo and behold, it was left untouched! Haha. I was lucky no one stole it. I thanked the guy who was manning the shop for letting me in. I went home happy.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-07-03',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Tragic Death of Chester Bennington',
            'description' => '<p>News regarding the death of Chester Bennington, the lead singer of Linkin Park, had broke out in Facebook today. At first, I thought it was a hoax. Later on, it was confirmed to be real. The media said he committed suicide by hanging himself. It\'s such a tragic loss in the music industry, as many people admire him. Plus, he\'s one of my favorite singers. Oh! The memories. His music shall live forever. Rest in peace.</p><p>I bought a G-Tec ballpen today. It\'s the 3rd G-Tec ballpen I have at the moment. My 2 previous ballpens had broken leads, despite the ink not being fully consumed. We had our Capstone system checked by our adviser, Ma\'am Josephine. It\'s the 2nd time we had it checked this trimester. We fulfilled her request of adding synonyms to our Essay Checker System to improve the features of the system. She "approved" the system and handed our documentation. We aren\'t endorsed yet. We have to come back on Monday next week for the progress of our documentation. Hopefully, we get endorsed for the final defense.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-07-21',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'New Haircut!',
            'description' => '<p>I sold my Wrangler pants for P200 through a meetup in Victory Liner at Upper Engineers\' Hill. After the transaction, I scheduled a 3 PM appointment at Stache. I seriously need a haircut! It\'s very long already. I went to the market to buy pork chop, tocino, bacon, longganisa and chicken wings then I went home (I nearly ran out of budget). At home, Patrick woke up early. He wants to have lunch at the carinderia by the road. My treat. I ordered an Ampalaya Rice for P35 while Patrick ordered a Giniling Rice for P45. I went out again.</p><p>I arrived in UC at 12:49 PM. The UC Gym is full of SHS students (there\'s an orientation regarding their school calendar). Me and Wendell were supposed to claim the finished bookbind at Bensa. When we went there, Wendell was told that we return at 3 PM since they haven\'t finished it yet. I told Wendell to claim it alone because I have an appointment at Stache. I left UC and walked all the way going to Stache despite a heavy rainfall. It\'s my 2nd time to have my haircut at Stache (my 1st time was way back on November 15, 2016). For the 1st time in 3 years, I opted for a new hairstyle. I showed a picture to my barber of what hairstyle I want. During the haircut, I opted to take all 3 optional services: trimming my facial hair, making the sideburns neat and going for a shampoo treatment. Lo and behold, I have a new, sleek and cool hairstyle! It\'s called "Quiff with Short Tapered Fade". I walked home.</p><p>At home, Patrick was the 1st person to notice my new hairstyle and commend me for a new look! Thanks, brother. To my surprise, Mama Cathy has arrived home. She was fetched by Tita Vina and Chloe. I was shocked! Mama called me at 6:35 PM. She knew that Mama Cathy has arrived home. Mama spoke to Lola, Tatay, and Megan.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-08-18',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'SM\'s Baskets',
            'description' => '<p>I went to town at around 9:30 AM and walked up going to Prime Hotel. I sold my Rotring drawing tube for P50. I went to UC to return my toga set that I rented for the 71st Commencement Exercise on August 31. The P500 deposit was refunded when I availed the toga set last August 23. They let me keep the tassel. I went home and took a little rest.</p><p>Me, Mama and Daddy went to SM using Tatay\'s vehicle. Me and Mama went ahead while Daddy looked for a parking space. We have a few things to do. One, we went to Mr. Quickie to repair one of Lola\'s bags as well as claim the 2 bags we sent yesterday. Second, we went to Globe to request for an upgrade of my 11-year old Globe SIM. We were there at 2:36 PM and waited until 3:19 PM. Once we got our turn, Mama spoke English to the CSR assisting me. She was shocked! Haha. Classic Mama right there! Third, we went to Seen to buy new eyeglasses and contact lenses. Daddy eventually showed up and told me that he\'ll wait for us at the veranda. I had a free eye check-up for the 1st time in so many years. My vision got worse than before. It is now -5.25 on both eyes compared to -5.00 (left) and -4.50 (right). Sad life. Fourth, we headed to Foodcourt to eat because Mama is hungry. Mama had Bibimbap while Daddy had Bicol Express. I ordered a 2-piece Honey Chicken at Oriental Bowl. Man, it was so delicious! We went down to the parking lot and Mama nabbed 2 SM baskets that weren\'t returned. Luckily, no one saw us.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-09-02',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Just Games and Food',
            'description' => '<p>Forge of Empires is so addicting. It\'s my 17th day playing this web browser game (I\'ve returned playing since August 31). I started playing it way back in 2014 along with Zedrick. Apparently, he doesn\'t play the game anymore and has been inactive ever since. I built 2 great buildings today. Observatory (a good-producing building that\'s sent to the guild treasury) and Statue of Zeus (provides military bonuses when attacking other players).</p><p>After playing Forge of Empires, I played Digimon Story Cyber Sleuth in the PS4. 19 Digimon medals were acquired today. I already have 492 medals and I need 8 more medals to nab the trophy "Legendary Medal Collector" (Silver). Mama cooked Adobong Baboy for our dinner tonight. Ah, Mama never falters in looking after us.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-09-17',
        ]);

        Post::create([
            'category_id' => 2,
            'user_id' => 1,
            'title' => 'Government Requirements Duties',
            'description' => '<p>Tried something new today. I wore a black v-neck shirt, a dark blue polo, dark blue Uniqlo pants and a black World Balance checkered shoes. It\'s my 1st time to wear an opened polo shirt with a v-neck shirt acting as an undershirt. I brought my USB with me. Time to go to town! I went to Gov. Pack to have my NBI Clearance and Birth Certificate photocopied. I was able to claim my NBI Clearance 3 days ago. While I\'m at it, I had the 2 documents scanned and placed in my USB for future use. The photocopied documents is what I will submit on my November 14 interview in Narda\'s at 10 AM. I went to 7-11 to buy a Gatorade drink as I got thirsty.</p><p>I went home to have lunch. Spam is my meal. After eating, I went to town again at around 3:30 PM to apply for a Postal ID. However, I found out that it\'s closed. It only opens during weekdays between 9 AM - 5 PM. I went home immediately.</p>',
            'created_at' => Carbon::parse('September 27, 2018 00:00:00')->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
            'date_published' => '2017-11-11',
        ]);

